hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18001","(913) — Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Allah al-Kafani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-ughlutat (captious, problematic questions)."
"18002","Atiyyah ibn Abi Jamilah Abu Hazzan from Muawiyah (914) — Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, Atiyyah Abu Hazzan narrated to me that he heard Muawiyah (report) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: I am only a conveyor and Allah guides, and a distributor and Allah gives; so whoever receives something from me with good conduct and wholesome desire, that is the one who is blessed in it, and whoever receives something with bad conduct and bad desire, that is the one who eats and is not satisfied."
"18003","(915) — Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us (H). And Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Fadl ibn Fadalalah, that Abu Hazzan Atiyyah ibn Abi Jamilah narrated to them, tracing it back to Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, and Muawiyah tracing it back to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I am only a conveyor and Allah guides, and I am only a distributor and Allah gives; so whoever receives something from us with good conduct and wholesome desire, that is the one who is blessed in it, and whoever receives something from us with bad conduct and bad desire, that is the one who eats and is not satisfied."
"18004","Abu al-Zahiriyyah Hudayr ibn Kurayb from Muawiyah (916) — Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am only a conveyor and Allah guides, and a distributor and Allah gives; so whoever receives something from me with good conduct and wholesome desire, that is the one who is blessed in it, and whoever receives something from me with bad desire and bad conduct, that is the one who eats and is not satisfied."
"18005","Numayr ibn Aws from Muawiyah (917) — Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, my father narrated to me (H). And Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, Numayr ibn Aws narrated to us that Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan used to say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will always remain of my ummah an ummah established upon the command of Allah; neither those who oppose them nor those who forsake them will harm them, until the command of Allah comes while they are dominant over people."
"18006","(918) — Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, my father narrated to us (H). And Umarah ibn Wathimah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, Numayr ibn Aws narrated to us that Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan used to say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"18007","(919) — Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, my father narrated to us (H). And Umarah ibn Wathimah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salim narrated to us, Numayr ibn Aws narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, that Muawiyah, the Commander of the Faithful, used to say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him."
"18008","Yazid ibn Sufyan from Muawiyah (920) — Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Saiqah narrated to me, al-Walid ibn Salih al-Nahhas narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Sufyan, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, forbidding riding upon the skins of predators and plastering (raising high) buildings."
"18009","Amr ibn Qays al-Sakuni from Muawiyah (921) — Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi and Abu Imran Musa ibn Sahl al-Jawni and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Amr ibn Qays narrated to us that he heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan on the pulpit cite this verse: {This day I have perfected for you your religion} — until he completed the verse, saying: It was revealed on the day of Arafah on a Friday. Then he recited this verse: {So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him do righteous deeds and not associate anyone in the worship of his Lord}. And he said: It is the last verse to be revealed."
"18010","Abu al-Fayd from Muawiyah (922) — Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Fayd, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"18011","Makhul from Muawiyah (923) — Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah, from Makhul who said: I heard Muawiyah on the pulpit say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he finished the prayer, would say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the wealth of the wealthy does not avail him against You."
"18012","Among those who narrated from Muawiyah of the people of Egypt: Rashid ibn Abi Sukaynah from Muawiyah (924) — Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from al-Yasa ibn Yaqub, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Rashid who said: I heard Muawiyah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, whomever I cursed in the pre-Islamic ignorance and who then entered Islam, make that a means of nearness to You for him."
"18013","Abu Qabil Hayy ibn Hani from Muawiyah (925) — Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Dimam ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Qabil relate from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan that he ascended the pulpit on Friday and said in his sermon: Wealth is our wealth, and the war-spoils (fay) are our spoils; whomever we wish we give, and whomever we wish we withhold. No one answered him. When the second Friday came he said the same, and no one answered him. When the third Friday came he said the same, and a man among those present in the mosque stood up to him and said: Nay! Wealth is our wealth and the spoils are our spoils; whoever stands between us and it, we shall bring him to judgment before Allah with our swords. Muawiyah descended and sent for the man and brought him in. The people said: The man is ruined! Then the people entered and found the man with him on the couch, and Muawiyah said to the people: This man has given me life; may Allah give him life. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be leaders after me who will speak and will not be answered, plunging into the Fire as monkeys plunge into it. I spoke on the first Friday and no one answered me, so I feared I was among them. Then I spoke on the second Friday and no one answered me, so I said to myself: I am of the people! Then I spoke on the third Friday and this man stood and answered me, so he gave me life; may Allah give him life."
"18014","Uqbah from Muawiyah (926) — Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Hunayn ibn Abi Hakim, that Abu Ubaydah ibn Uqbah narrated to him, from his father, from Muawiyah, that he said: Fasting while travelling is not of the Sunnah."
"18015","(927) — Abu Ghassan Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn al-Walid al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Nahshal al-Tamimi, that he heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say many times: When the caller to prayer calls and testifies, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) testified as he testified; then when he said: Come to prayer, he said: There is no power and no strength except through Allah; and when he said: Come to success, he likewise said: There is no power and no strength except through Allah."
"18016","Unnamed men from Muawiyah (928) — Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to me, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir who said: One who heard Muawiyah narrated to me, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat milk, then he stood and prayed without performing ablution."
"18017","(929) — Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Utbah ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, from one who narrated to him, from Muawiyah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O people, knowledge is only through learning, and understanding is only through seeking understanding; whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion; and only the scholars among His servants fear Allah."
"18018","(930) — Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Fadl ibn Mubashshir, from his uncle, from Muawiyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten houses in the Hijaz endure longer than twenty houses in Syria."
"18019","(931) — Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Sad al-Dashtaki narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abu Umayyah al-Thaqafi, from a man, from his uncle who said: Muawiyah came out to us after we had prayed the noon prayer while we were supplicating to Allah, and said: Stay in your places until I come to you! Then he came out to us having covered himself with a cloak, and when he had prayed the afternoon prayer he said: Shall I not narrate to you something the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did? They prayed with him the first (noon) prayer, then sat until they prayed with him the afternoon prayer, and he came out to them and said: You have not left yet? They said: No. He said: If you could see your Lord, blessed and exalted, opening a gate of the gates of heaven, boasting to His angels of your gatherings while you await the prayer."
"18020","(932) — Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Jarir narrated to us, saying: I heard an old man narrating to Mughirah, from the daughter of Hisham ibn al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah — and she used to nurse Ammar ibn Yasir — who said: Muawiyah entered upon Ammar, and when he came out from him he said: O Allah, do not make his death at our hands, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The rebellious party will kill Ammar."
"18021","Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam (933) — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam, that the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, among us are men who take evil omens! He said: That is something you find in yourselves, and it will not harm you! They said: And among us are men who go to soothsayers! He said: Then do not go to a soothsayer."
"18022","(934) — Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about omens, and he said: That is something you find in yourselves, and it shall never harm you."
"18023","(935) — Abu Usamah Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani al-Rusafi narrated to us, saying: My grandfather narrated to me, from al-Zuhri who said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami — and he was among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you see things we used to do in the pre-Islamic ignorance? We used to take evil omens! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is something one of you finds in himself, so let it never turn you back! I said: O Messenger of Allah, and we used to go to soothsayers! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then do not go to soothsayers."
"18024","(936) — Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Marwan al-Uthmani narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam, the same as the hadith of Malik: concerning the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), eleven rakahs, and his lying on his right side."
"18025","Chapter: Ata ibn Yasar from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam (937) — Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to me, Ata ibn Yasar narrated to me, Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami narrated to me, saying: I went out to a flock tended by a slave-girl of mine in the direction of Uhud and al-Jawwaniyyah, and found that a wolf had taken a sheep from it. And I am a man of the sons of Adam who feels grief as they feel grief! So I struck her a blow, then turned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he deemed it grave against me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not free her? He said: Yes, bring her to me! So I brought her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Where is Allah? She said: Allah, mighty and majestic, is in the heaven. He said: Then who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: She is a believer, so free her."
"18026","(938) — Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me (H). And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us — both saying: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami who said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I had a slave-girl who tended small sheep in the direction of Uhud; when I looked over her I found that a wolf had taken a sheep from them. And I am of the sons of Adam who feels grief as they feel grief, but I struck her a blow, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) deemed it grave against me. So I said: Shall I not free her? He said: Bring her to me! So I brought her, and he said: Where is Allah? She said: In the heaven. He said: Who am I? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Free her, for she is a believer."
"18027","(939) — Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam who said: I had a slave-girl who tended small sheep toward Uhud — and he mentioned the hadith."
"18028","(940) — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, among us are men who take evil omens! He said: That is something you find in yourselves, and it will not harm you! He said: I said: And among us are men who go to soothsayers! He said: Do not go to them. He said: And among us are men who draw lines (for divination)! He said: A prophet drew lines, so whoever matches his knowledge, knows."
"18029","(941) — Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to me, Ata ibn Yasar narrated to me, Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami narrated to me, saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we have recently left the pre-Islamic ignorance and Allah has brought Islam, and men among us take evil omens! He said: That is something they find in their breasts, so let it never turn them back! He said: O Messenger of Allah, and men among us go to soothsayers! He said: No, do not go to them. He said: And men among us draw lines! He said: A prophet among the prophets used to draw lines, so whoever matches his line, that is it."
"18030","(942) — Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, among us are men who take evil omens! He said: That is something you find in your breasts, and it will not harm you. I said: And among us are men who go to soothsayers! He said: Then do not go to them. I said: And among us are men who draw lines! He said: A prophet drew lines, so whoever matches his knowledge, knows."
"18031","(943) — Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me (H). And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us — both saying: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a people recently of the pre-Islamic ignorance, and Allah has brought Islam, and among us are men who go to soothsayers! He said: Then do not go to them. I said: And among us are men who take evil omens! He said: That is something they find in their breasts, and it will not harm them. I said: And among us are men who draw lines! He said: A prophet among the prophets used to draw lines, so whoever matches his line, that is it."
"18032","(944) — Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Muqad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to me, Ata ibn Yasar narrated to me that Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami narrated to him, saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a people recently of the pre-Islamic ignorance, and Allah, mighty and majestic, has brought Islam, and men among us draw lines! He said: A prophet among the prophets used to draw lines, so whoever matches his line, that is it. He said: And among us are men who take evil omens! He said: That is something they find in their breasts, but it will not harm them. I said: And among us are men who go to soothsayers! He said: Then do not go to them."
"18033","(945) — Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, Ata ibn Yasar narrated to me, Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami narrated to me, saying: While I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man among the people sneezed, and I said: May Allah have mercy on you. The people stared at me with their eyes. I said: Woe to my mother, what is wrong with you that you look at me? He said: The people struck their hands upon their thighs, and when I saw them silencing me I fell silent. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished — may my father and mother be sacrificed for him; I never saw a teacher before him nor after him better in teaching than him; by Allah he did not strike me, nor rebuke me harshly, nor revile me — but he said: This prayer of ours, nothing of the speech of people is proper in it; it is only glorification, magnification, and recitation of the Quran."
"18034","(946) — Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man among the people sneezed. And he mentioned the hadith."
"18035","(947) — Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us (H). And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us — both saying: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man among the people sneezed, and I said: May Allah have mercy on you! The people cast their eyes at me, and I said: Woe to my mother, what is the matter with you that you look at me? They began striking their hands upon their thighs, and I knew they were silencing me, but I fell silent. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed — may my father and mother be sacrificed for him — he did not strike me, nor rebuke me harshly, nor revile me. Then he said: This prayer, nothing of this speech of people is lawful in it; it is only glorification, magnification, and recitation of the Quran — or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"18036","(948) — Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Al-Hasan ibn Qazaah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man among the people sneezed, and I said: May Allah have mercy on you! — or: May Allah have mercy on you all! The people looked at me, and I said: Woe to my mother! Then they stared at me and began striking their hands upon their thighs, and I knew that the people were glaring at me with their eyes. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer — may my father and mother be sacrificed for him; I never saw a teacher before or after him gentler in teaching than him — he did not scold me, nor rebuke me harshly, nor revile me, but said: This prayer, nothing of the speech of people is proper in it; it is only glorification, magnification, and recitation of the Quran. And Ayyub did not mention Ata ibn Yasar in his hadith."
"18037","Muawiyah ibn Haydah al-Qushayri (949) — Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Qanab ibn al-Muharrar narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Adi narrated to us: Muawiyah ibn Haydah ibn Qushayr ibn Kab ibn Rabiah ibn Amir ibn Sasah."
"18038","Bahz ibn Hakim from his father from his grandfather (950) — Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the one who speaks and makes his people laugh by lying; woe to him, woe to him."
"18039","(951) — Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us (H). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us — both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the one who speaks and lies in order to make the people laugh by it; woe to him, woe to him."
"18040","(952) — Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He who narrates to people and lies in order to make the people laugh by it — woe to him, woe to him."
"18041","(953) — Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed me, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the one who narrates to people lying in order to make them laugh; woe to him, woe to him."
"18042","(954) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, to the one who narrates to the people and makes them laugh: Woe to him, woe to him."
"18043","(955) — Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18044","(956) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18045","(957) — Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, to whom should I show kindness? He said: Your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your father, then the nearest, then the nearest."
"18046","(958) — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, to whom should I show kindness? He said: Your mother — saying it three times. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then to whom should I show kindness? He said: Your father. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then whom? He said: Then the nearest, then the nearest."
"18047","(959) — Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us (H). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us — both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, to whom should I show kindness? He said: Your mother, then your mother, then your mother, then your father, then the nearest, then the nearest."
"18048","(960) — Yaqub ibn Khalifah al-Abbadani narrated to us, Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, Azhar ibn Sad narrated to me, from Ibn Awn, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, to whom should I show kindness? He said: Your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your father, then the nearest, then the nearest."
"18049","(961) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, to whom should I show kindness? He said: Your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your father. I said: Then whom? He said: Then the nearest, then the nearest."
"18050","(962) — Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun and Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18051","(963) — Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, to whom should I show kindness? He said: Your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Your father, then the nearest, then the nearest."
"18052","(964) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Isa ibn Yunus and al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed me, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18053","Chapter (965) — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we ask one another for our wealth among ourselves! He said: Yes, a man asks during strife between him and his people, and when he attains enough or nearly attains it, he refrains."
"18054","(966) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people who ask one another for our wealth among ourselves! He said: Let one of you ask in need and in strife to reconcile between his people; then when he attains enough or nearly attains it, he should be self-restrained."
"18055","(967) — Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18056","(968) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18057","Chapter (969) — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: By Allah, I did not come to you until I had sworn by the number of these fingers of mine that I would neither follow you nor follow your religion. And I have come to a man who understands nothing except what Allah — mighty and majestic — and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me, and I ask you by Allah: With what did your Lord send you to us? He said: Sit down. Then he said: With Islam. I said: And what is the sign of Islam? He said: That you testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), establish the prayer, give the zakah, and separate yourself from polytheism; and every Muslim is inviolable to another Muslim, two brothers, two helpers. Allah does not accept any deed from a polytheist who commits polytheism after his Islam. And my Lord will call me and ask me whether I conveyed to His servants; so let your witness convey to your absent one. And you will be called with muzzles placed over your mouths; and the first thing asked about one of you will be his thigh and his palm. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is this our religion? He said: Yes. You will be gathered upon your faces and upon your feet and riding."
"18058","(970) — Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he mentioned the same as the hadith of Mamar."
"18059","(971) — Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18060","(972) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim and al-Nadr ibn Shumayl and Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18061","(973) — Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will be called on the Day of Resurrection with your mouths muzzled; then he said: The first thing to speak from one of you will be his thigh and his palm."
"18062","(974) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will be gathered as men on foot and as riders, and dragged upon your faces."
"18063","(975) — Ahmad ibn Zakariyya al-Iyadi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Qays narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, choose (a land) for me! So he pointed with his hand toward Syria, and said: O people, you will be gathered as men on foot and as riders, and dragged upon your faces with your mouths muzzled; and the first thing to begin from one of you will be his thigh."
"18064","(976) — Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18065","(977) — Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18066","(978) — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is asked by his freedman for surplus wealth and does not give it to him, it will be transformed on the Day of Resurrection into a bald serpent."
"18067","(979) — Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar both said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one asks a freedman for a surplus that is with him and he withholds it, except that his surplus that is with him will come on the Day of Resurrection as a bald serpent."
"18068","(980) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man comes to his freedman and asks him for a surplus that is with him and he withholds it, except that Allah will make for him on the Day of Resurrection a bald serpent — the surplus which he withholds."
"18069","(981) — Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18070","(982) — Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18071","(983) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18072","Chapter (984) — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For every forty grazing camels, a bint labun (a two-year-old she-camel) is due; so whoever gives it seeking reward, for him is its reward, and whoever conceals it, we shall take it along with half of his camels as a binding decree from the decrees of your Lord. It is not lawful for Muhammad nor for the family of Muhammad."
"18073","(985) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every grazing camel, for every forty, a bint labun is due, and camels are not to be separated from their state; so whoever gives it seeking profit (reward), for him is its reward, and whoever withholds it, I shall take it along with half of his wealth as a decree from the decrees of our Lord. There is nothing in it for the family of Muhammad."
"18074","(986) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For every grazing camel, for every forty, a bint labun is due; whoever brings it seeking reward, for him is its reward, and whoever withholds it, we shall take it along with half of his camels as a decree from the decrees of our Lord. Nothing of it is lawful for the family of Muhammad."
"18075","(987) — Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak and Yazid ibn Harun and Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18076","(988) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Isa ibn Yunus and al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18077","Chapter (989) — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, of our private parts, what may we approach and what should we leave? He said: Guard your private part except from your wife and what your right hand possesses. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if some are with others? He said: If you are able that no one sees your private part, then do so. They said: If one of us is alone by himself? He said: Allah is more deserving that modesty be shown to Him — and he placed his hand over his private part."
"18078","(990) — Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan informed, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, of our private parts, what may we approach and what should we leave? He said: Guard your private part except from your wife or what your right hand possesses. I said: What if some of us are with others? He said: If you are able that no one sees your private part, then do so. I said: What do you say if one of us is sitting alone? He said: Allah is more deserving that modesty be shown to Him."
"18079","(991) — Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us (H). And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us — both saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, of our private parts, what may we approach and what should we leave? He said: Cover your private part except from your wife or what your right hand possesses. Al-Hajabi added in his hadith: I said: The people, some of them with others? He said: If you are able that no one sees it, then do not show it. I said: What if one of us is alone? He said: Then Allah is more deserving that modesty be shown to Him."
"18080","(992) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, of our private parts, what may we approach and what should we leave? He said: Guard your private part except from your wife and what your right hand possesses. I said: What if we are, some of us with others? He said: Guard your private part as much as you can. (I asked:) What if we are in seclusion? He said: Allah is more deserving that modesty be shown to Him."
"18081","(993) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, of our private parts, what may we approach and what should we leave? He said: Guard your private part except from your wife or what your right hand possesses. I said: When the people are, some of them with others? He said: If you are able that no one ever sees it, then let no one see it. I said: O Prophet of Allah, what about one of us when alone? He said: Then Allah is more deserving that modesty be shown to Him."
"18082","(994) — Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun and Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18083","(995) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus and al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18084","Chapter (996) — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized some people of my tribe on suspicion, and a man of my tribe came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was delivering a sermon, and said: O Muhammad, for what do you detain my neighbours? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent. He said: Some people say that you forbid a thing and (yet) deem it lawful for yourself! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are you saying? So I began to intervene between them with speech, fearing that he would hear it and supplicate against my tribe with a supplication after which they would never prosper. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued until he understood it, then said: They have said it — or he said: He said it concerning them — by Allah, had I done it, it would be against me and not against them. Release his neighbours for him."
"18085","(997) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18086","(998) — Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) detained a man on suspicion, and he was spoken to concerning him, so he released him."
"18087","Chapter (999) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, of our women, what may we approach and what should we leave? He said: Your tilth — so come to your tilth as you wish — except that you do not strike the face, nor revile, nor forsake except in the house; and feed (her) when you eat, and clothe (her) when you clothe yourself, since some of you have intimately approached others."
"18088","(1000) — Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, of our women, what may we approach and what should we leave? He said: Your tilth — come to your tilth as you wish — except that you do not strike the face, nor revile, nor forsake except in the house; and feed (her) when you eat, and clothe (her) when you clothe yourself, since some of you have intimately approached others."
"18089","(1001) — Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18090","(1002) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18091","(1003) — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Karimah al-Basri and Abdan ibn Ahmad both said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Waqid al-Bahili, al-Wuhaymah, narrated to us, Abu Habib al-Qanawi narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three eyes shall not see the Fire: an eye that kept watch in the path of Allah, an eye that wept from fear of Allah, and an eye that lowered itself from the prohibitions of Allah."
"18092","(1004) — Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Durust narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A black fertile woman is better than a beautiful one who does not bear children. I shall vie in numbers with you against the nations, even with the miscarried foetus who will remain leaning at the gate of Paradise; it will be said to him: Enter Paradise! He will say: O Lord, and my parents? It will be said to him: Enter Paradise, you and your parents."
"18093","(1005) — Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Mukhayyis ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah said: I am with the opinion My servant holds of Me."
"18094","(1006) — Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari and Abdan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Ammar, Mikhyas ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah the Exalted created a hundred mercies; one mercy is among His creation by which they show mercy to one another, and He has stored away ninety-nine for His allies."
"18095","(1007) — Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Mikhyas ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Anger spoils matters as vinegar spoils honey."
"18096","(1008) — Abdan ibn Ahmad and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari both said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ali ibn Ibrahim and Abd Allah ibn Salamah narrated to us — both from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when charity was brought to him, would not eat from it, and when a gift was brought to him, he would eat from it."
"18097","(1009) — Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Sulami narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be brought food; if it was charity he would not eat from it, and if it was a gift he would eat from it."
"18098","(1010) — Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, al-Jarud ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you restrain yourselves from mentioning the sinner? Mention him by what is in him so that people may know him."
"18099","(1011) — Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Judubah ibn Yahya al-Laythi narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Bishr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no backbiting of a sinner."
"18100","(1012) — Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Isa al-Juhani narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; you are eighty rows and the rest of mankind is the remainder; and you complete seventy nations — you are the best of them and the most honoured of them to Allah, mighty and majestic."
"18101","(1013) — Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Salih al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hawtharah ibn Ashras narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever changes his religion, kill him. Allah does not accept the repentance of a servant who disbelieves after his Islam."
"18102","(1014) — Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Utbah ibn Said ibn al-Rakhs al-Himsi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of my neighbour upon me? He said: If he falls ill you visit him, if he dies you accompany his funeral, if he seeks a loan from you you lend him, if he is needy you cover him, if good befalls him you congratulate him, and if calamity befalls him you console him; and do not raise your building above his building so that you block the wind from him, and do not harm him with the smell of your cooking pot unless you ladle some of it for him."
"18103","(1015) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us (H). And Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us — both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to Syria."
"18104","(1016) — Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhram narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from his brother Mukhariq, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: From Allah, mighty and majestic — not from His Messenger — may Allah curse the cutter of the lote-tree."
"18105","(1017) — Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Haruthi narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no power and no strength except through Allah is a treasure among the treasures of Paradise."
"18106","(1018) — Ahmad ibn Masud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us (H). And al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Tusi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abd Allah, from al-Asbagh, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Secret charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord."
"18107","(1019) — Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Mamar narrated to us, Masadah ibn al-Yasa narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbours; to which of them should I give a gift? He said: To the one of them whose door is nearer to you."
"18108","(1020) — Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Attab al-Sukkari narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Mamar Abu al-Fadl narrated to us, Ali ibn Masadah al-Bahili narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbours; to which of them should I give a gift? He said: To the one of them whose door is nearer to you."
"18109","(1021) — Ahmad ibn Mabharam al-Idhaji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Ghassan Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, Awn ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {That Day Allah will pay them in full their true recompense} — thus he said."
"18110","(1022) — Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Ghassan ibn Malik al-Sulami narrated to us, Awn ibn Dhakwan Abu Janab al-Qassab narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping his hand over his thigh and saying: {That Day Allah will pay them in full their true recompense, and they will know that Allah is the Manifest Truth}."
"18111","(1023) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You complete seventy nations; you are the best of them and the most honoured of them to Allah, mighty and majestic."
"18112","(1024) — Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18113","(1025) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to me, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18114","Chapter (1026) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There was a servant among the servants of Allah to whom Allah gave wealth and children; part of his life passed and part remained. He said to his sons: What kind of father was I to you? They said: A good father. He said: By Allah, I shall not leave with anyone any wealth of mine owed to him except that I shall take it, or you do to me what I tell you! So he took a covenant from them. He said: Then no — rather, see: when I die, burn me with fire, then grind me, then see a windy day and scatter me, so that I may escape Allah! He said: So he was summoned and gathered, and it was said to him: What carried you to do what you did? He said: Fear of Your punishment! He said: Go forth forgiven — and he was pardoned."
"18115","(1027) — Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There was a servant among the servants of Allah whom Allah gave wealth — and he mentioned the same."
"18116","(1028) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18117","(1029) — Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same."
"18118","Said ibn Hakim ibn Muawiyah from his father; Said al-Jurayri from Hakim ibn Muawiyah (1030) — Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You complete seventy nations; you are the last of them and the most honoured of them to Allah, mighty and majestic."
"18119","(1031) — Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You will come on the Day of Resurrection with muzzles upon your mouths; and the first thing to speak from a person will be his thigh and his palm."
"18120","(1032) — Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is the sea of water and the sea of wine and the sea of milk and the sea of honey; then the rivers split off thereafter."
"18121","Yahya ibn Jabir al-Tai from Hakim ibn Muawiyah (1033) — Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Said ibn Sinan, from Yahya ibn Jabir al-Tai, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, with what has our Lord sent you to us? He said: That you worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish the prayer, give the zakah, and every Muslim is inviolable to another Muslim. This is your religion; wherever you are, it suffices you."
"18122","Abu Qazaah Suwayd ibn Hujayr from Hakim ibn Muawiyah (1034) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us (H). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us — both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Abu Qazaah, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of the wife of one of us upon him? He said: He feeds her when he eats, clothes her when he clothes himself, does not strike the face, and does not forsake her except in the house."
"18123","(1035) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Qazaah al-Bahili, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept the repentance of a servant who commits polytheism after his Islam."
"18124","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no freedman who comes to a freedman of his and asks him for some of his surplus and he withholds it from him, except that Allah makes it a serpent against its owner, biting him."
"18125","(1036) — Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Qazaah, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not come to you until I had sworn by the number of these fingers of mine that I would not come to you. By the One who sent you with the truth, with what has Allah sent you? He said: With Islam. I said: What is Islam? He said: That you submit your heart to Allah, turn your face to Allah, pray the obligatory prayer, and pay the obligatory zakah — two brothers, two helpers. Allah does not accept the repentance of a servant who commits polytheism after his Islam."
"18126","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You will be gathered here — and he gestured with his hand toward al-Sham — on foot and mounted and on your faces; you will be presented before Allah with muzzles (al-fidam) over your mouths, and the first thing that will speak on behalf of one of you will be his thigh."
"18127","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You will complete seventy nations; you are the last of them and the noblest of them before Allah."
"18128","1037 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqall al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us — both said: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj al-Bahili narrated to me, Suwayd ibn Hujayr narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I swore by the number of these — and he gestured to his fingers — that I would neither follow you nor follow what you brought, so I ask you by Allah, what is this religion of yours with which Allah sent you? He said: He sent me with Islam. I said: What is Islam? He said: That you say: I have submitted myself to Allah and turned my face to Him, and you establish prayer and give zakah, two supporting brothers; no repentance is accepted from one who associates partners with Allah after his Islam. I said: What is the right of our wives over us? He said: Feed her when you eat, and clothe her when you clothe yourself, and do not strike the face nor revile, nor forsake except in the house. Then he said: Here you will be gathered — and he gestured toward al-Sham — on foot and mounted, and dragged on your faces; you will come to Allah on the day you come to Him with muzzles over your mouths, and the first thing that will speak on behalf of one of you will be his thigh. You will complete seventy nations; you are the last of them and the noblest of them before Allah. And there is no patron who comes to a patron asking him for some surplus he has and he withholds it from him except that it will come to him on the Day of Resurrection as a venomous serpent gaping its mouth. And there was a man among those before you whom Allah had granted wealth and children until one generation passed and one remained, and when death came to him he said to his family: What kind of man was I to you? They said: The best of men. He said: Either I take back everything I gave you or you do what I command you. They said: We will all do what you command us. He said: When I die, burn me in fire, and when I become charcoal crush me then scatter me on a windy day. So Allah summoned him as he had been, and said: What carried you to do what you did? He said: Fear of You, O Lord — so his Lord rescued him."
"18129","1038 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Shibl ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Qaza'ah narrating to Amr ibn Dinar, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of one of our wives over him? He said: You feed her when you eat, and clothe her when you clothe yourself, and do not strike the face, nor revile it, nor forsake except in the house. And he gestured with his hand toward al-Sham and said: Here you will be gathered, riding and on foot, on your faces on the Day of Resurrection, with muzzles over your mouths; and you will complete seventy nations, you are the last of them and the noblest of them before Allah; and the first thing that will speak on behalf of one of you will be his thigh."
"18130","1039 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Qaza'ah, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is the right of a wife over her husband? He said: He feeds her when he eats, and clothes her when he clothes himself, and does not strike the face nor revile, and does not forsake except in his house."
"18131","Muawiyah ibn Muawiyah al-Muzani; he died during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his bier was raised before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he prayed over him. 1040 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham the mu'adhdhin narrated to us, Mahbub ibn Hilal al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Jibril (peace be upon him) descended upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, Muawiyah ibn Muawiyah al-Muzani has died; would you like to pray over him? He said: Yes. So he struck with his wings and no tree nor hill remained but it shook, and his bier was raised for him until he looked at it, and he prayed over him with two rows of angels behind him, in each row seventy thousand. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jibril: O Jibril, what brought him to this station with Allah? He said: By his love of (Say: He is Allah, the One) and his recitation of it coming and going, standing and sitting, and in every state."
"18132","1041 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Mu'allim narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Abi Sahl narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Muawiyah ibn Muawiyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was campaigning at Tabuk when Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him and said: O Muhammad, would you join the funeral of Muawiyah ibn Muawiyah al-Muzani? He said: Yes. So Jibril gestured with his hand thus, and the mountains and hills were parted for him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came walking, with Jibril (peace be upon him) alongside him, and with Jibril were seventy thousand angels, and he prayed over Muawiyah ibn Muawiyah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jibril (peace be upon him): By what did Muawiyah attain this? He said: By his frequent recitation of (Say: He is Allah, the One); he used to recite it standing and sitting and lying and walking; this is what brought him to what he reached."
"18133","Muawiyah ibn Nawfal al-Dayli. 1042 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Abi Sabrah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nawfal ibn Muawiyah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That one of you be left without family and wealth is better for him than missing the time of the Asr prayer."
"18134","Muawiyah al-Laythi. 1043 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi and Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Harawi al-Basri narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Muawiyah al-Laythi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People wake up suffering drought, then Allah brings them provision from Himself, and they wake up as polytheists, saying: We were given rain by such-and-such a star."
"18135","Muawiyah ibn Hudayj al-Sakuni. 1044 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If there is healing in anything, it is in a drink of honey, or a cut of the cupper, or a branding with fire; and I do not love to be cauterized."
"18136","1045 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj and Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Bukayr al-Misri narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Urfutah ibn Amr al-Hadrami, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: An evening journey in the path of Allah or a morning journey is better than the world and what is in it."
"18137","1046 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A morning journey in the path of Allah or an evening journey is better than the world and what is in it."
"18138","1047 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A morning journey in the path of Allah or an evening journey is better than the world and what is in it."
"18139","1048 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, (Ha). And Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us — both said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj who said: I prayed Maghrib with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he forgot and gave salam after two rak'ahs, then left. A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you forgot and gave salam after two rak'ahs. So he ordered Bilal who gave the iqamah, then he completed that rak'ah. The people asked about the man who had said: O Messenger of Allah, you forgot. It was said: Do you know him? I said: No, unless I see him — then he passed by me and I said: This is he. They said: This is Talhah ibn Ubaydillah."
"18140","Those named Muslim. Muslim al-Khuza'i. 1049 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, (Ha). And Ali ibn al-Wazir al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Makki narrated to us, (Ha). And Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us — they said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Amr ibn Muslim al-Khuza'i narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I recited to him the verse of Suwayd ibn Amir al-Mustaliqi — Yamani — so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had this man met me he would have become Muslim. Then my father wept, so I said: O father, what makes you weep over a polytheist who died in the Jahiliyyah? He said: I never saw any good among the polytheists better than Suwayd."
"18141","Muslim, Abu Ra'itah. 1050 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi and Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Sinan al-Awaqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Abza al-Makki narrated to us, my mother Ra'itah bint Muslim narrated to me, from her father who said: I was present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Hunayn, and he said: What is your name? I said: Ghurab (crow). He said: You are Muslim."
"18142","Muslim ibn al-Harith ibn Badal al-Tamimi. 1051 - Musa ibn Sahl Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan al-Kinani narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Muslim al-Tamimi narrated to me that his father narrated to him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray the dawn prayer, say before you speak to anyone: O Allah, grant me refuge from the Fire — seven times; for if you die that day, protection from the Fire will be written for you. And when you pray Maghrib, say the like before you speak to anyone; for if you die that night, protection from the Fire will be written for you."
"18143","1052 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, (Ha). And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us — both said: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan, al-Harith ibn Muslim al-Tamimi narrated to us, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on a detachment, and when we attacked the people I went ahead of my companions on my horse, and the women and children came out wailing. I said to them: Do you wish to save yourselves? They said: Yes. I said: Say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger — so they said it. Then my companions came and blamed me, saying: We were on the verge of booty and you deprived us. Then we returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: You do not know what he has done; Allah has written for him such-and-such reward for every person — then he drew me near him and said: When you pray the dawn prayer, say before you speak to anyone: O Allah, grant me refuge from the Fire — seven times; for if you die that day Allah will write for you thereby protection from the Fire. And when you pray Maghrib, say before you speak to anyone: O Allah, grant me refuge from the Fire — seven times; for if you die that night Allah will write for you protection from the Fire."
"18144","1053 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan al-Kinani narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Muslim al-Tamimi narrated to us, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for him a letter of counsel to those after him among whom Allah entrusts the affair, and sealed it."
"18145","Muslim ibn Abd al-Rahman. 1054 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqall al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir al-Ramli narrated to us, from Shamsiyyah bint Nabhan, from her patron Muslim ibn Abd al-Rahman who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taking the pledge of the women in the year of the Conquest at al-Safa. A woman whose hand was like a man's hand spoke, and he refused to take her pledge until she went and changed her hand with yellow dye. And a man came to him wearing an iron ring, and he said: Allah does not purify a hand in which there is an iron ring."
"18146","Muslim ibn Aslam ibn Bajrah al-Ansari, then al-Khazraji. 1055 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Muslim ibn Aslam ibn Bajrah, the brother of al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj — and he was a very old shaykh who had resolved within himself, he said: He would enter Madinah and fulfil his need in the market, then return to his family; and when he put down his cloak he would remember that he had not prayed in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and would say: By Allah, I have not prayed in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for he said to us: Whoever among you comes down to this town, let him not return to his family until he prays two rak'ahs in this mosque, then returns to his family."
"18147","1056 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Aslam ibn Bajrah, from his father, from his grandfather Aslam ibn Bajrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put him in charge of the captives of Qurayzah, and he would look at the front of a boy; if he saw that hair had grown, his neck was struck, and if not, he placed him among the spoils of the Muslims."
"18148","Muslim, Abu Awsajah. 1057 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkani narrated to me, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Awsajah ibn Muslim, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinate, then perform wudu and wipe over his khuffs."
"18149","Muslim ibn Umayr al-Thaqafi. 1058 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Nu'man al-Bahili narrated to us, Muzahim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Umayr narrated to us, he said: A green jar containing camphor was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he divided it among the Muhajirun and the Ansar, and said: O Umm Sulaym, make nabidh for us in it."
"18150","Muslim ibn al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami. 1059 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mabahram al-Idhaji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Raqqi narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Talhah ibn Muslim ibn al-Ala al-Hadrami narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Muslim who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what he instructed al-Ala when he sent him to al-Bahrayn; he said: It is not lawful for anyone to be ignorant of the obligations and the sunan, and lawful for him is what is besides that. And he wrote for al-Ala: Apply to the Magians the practice (sunnah) of the People of the Book."
"18151","Those named Maslamah. Maslamah ibn Makhlad al-Ansari; of his reports: and he is Maslamah ibn Makhlad ibn al-Samit ibn Niyar ibn Ludhan ibn Abd Wudd ibn Zayd ibn Tha'labah ibn al-Khazraj ibn Sa'idah ibn Ka'b ibn al-Khazraj. 1060 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Sha'tha Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ulayy, from his father who said: I heard Ibn Makhlad say: I was born when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, and he died when I was ten years old."
"18152","1061 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah, from his father, from Maslamah ibn Mukhallad who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived when I was four years old, and he died when I was fourteen. And the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi is in my view the correct one, and Allah knows best."
"18153","1062 - Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: In the year sixty-two Maslamah ibn Makhlad died."
"18154","What Maslamah ibn Makhlad transmitted. 1063 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Mujammi' ibn Ka'b, from Maslamah ibn Mukhallad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep women without adornment so that they stay in their chambers."
"18155","1064 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, (Ha). And Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us — both said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abu Hani narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Malik, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj, from Maslamah ibn Mukhallad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muhajirun will precede the people by forty autumns (years) to Paradise, enjoying bliss therein while the people are detained for reckoning; then the second company will be after a hundred autumns."
"18156","1065 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah, from Maslamah ibn Mukhallad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muawiyah: O Allah, give him authority in the lands and protect him from the evil of punishment."
"18157","1066 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Hilal al-Rasibi, from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah, from Maslamah ibn Mukhallad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muawiyah: O Allah, teach him the Book and reckoning, and give him authority in the lands."
"18158","1067 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi, from Ibn Awn, from Makhul, that Uqbah ibn Amir came to Maslamah ibn Mukhallad, and there was something between him and the doorkeeper, so he heard his voice and gave him permission. He said: I did not come to you as a visitor, but I came to you with a need. Do you remember the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever knows a misdeed of his brother and conceals it, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Yes. He said: For this I came."
"18159","Those named Ma'n. Ma'n ibn Yazid al-Sulami; of his reports: 1068 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: I heard Bakkar ibn Muhammad ibn Wasi' say: Muawiyah said: No Qurashi woman has borne to a Qurashi man one better for her in her religion than Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no Qurashi woman has borne to a Qurashi man one better for her in her worldly life than me. So Ma'n ibn Yazid al-Sulami said: No Qurashi woman has borne to a Qurashi man one better for her in her religion than Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no Qurashi woman has borne to a Qurashi man worse for her in her worldly life than you. He said: Why? He said: Because you accustomed them to a habit, and it is as if I see them seeking it from other than you, so it will bring them fallen dead in the roads. He said: Woe to you; by Allah, I have been concealing it from myself for such-and-such a time."
"18160","What Ma'n ibn Yazid al-Sulami transmitted. 1069 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Waddah ibn Yahya al-Nahshali narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Kulayb ibn Wa'il, from his father, from Ma'n ibn Yazid who said: A Bedouin came and took hold of the halter of the Prophet's camel (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, guide me to a deed that brings me near Paradise and distances me from the Fire. He said: You have been concise in your question though you asked at length: Worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, pray the five, fast Ramadan, and what you dislike people doing to you, dislike it for them."
"18161","1070 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Dhahabi narrated to us, (Ha). And Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us — both said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu al-Juwayriyah, from Ma'n ibn Yazid al-Sulami who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and my father and my grandfather; and he addressed (a proposal) on my behalf and married me, and I brought a dispute to him and he ruled in my favour. My father had come with two dinars to give in charity and placed them with a man, and I took them and brought them to him. He said: By Allah, I did not mean you. So I disputed with him before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: For you is what you intended, O Yazid, and for you, O Ma'n, is what you took."
"18162","1071 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from my grandfather, from Abu al-Juwayriyah, from Ma'n ibn Yazid who said: I brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he ruled in my favour; and he addressed (a proposal) on my behalf and married me, and I pledged allegiance to him, I and my grandfather."
"18163","1072 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu al-Juwayriyah, from Ma'n ibn Yazid who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and my grandfather; and I brought a dispute to him and he ruled in my favour, and he addressed (a proposal) on my behalf and married me. And Ma'n said: No spoils are lawful until they are divided, and do not take from them until they are divided among the people."
"18164","1073 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, (Ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Fahd ibn Awf Abu Rabi'ah narrated to us — both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abu al-Juwayriyah al-Jarmi who said: We were in the land of the Romans, and a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Banu Sulaym called Ma'n ibn Yazid al-Sulami was appointed over us. He said: I found a red jar containing dinars, so I brought it to him and he took the fifth from it, saying: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no extra allotment (nafal) except from the fifth — I would have given it to you. He said: Then he offered me some of his share, and I said: I have no need of it."
"18165","1074 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated to me, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq informed us, Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari informed me, from Asim al-Ahwal, Suhayl ibn Dhira' narrated to me that he heard Ma'n ibn Yazid say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather in your mosques, and when a people gather, let them inform me. So we gathered before all the people and came to him and informed him; he came walking with us until he sat with us. He said: Then a speaker among us spoke and said: Praise be to Allah, for whom there is no shortcoming below praise, and beyond whom there is no outlet — or something like this. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and stood up, and we blamed one another, and said: Allah singled us out by his coming to us before all the people, yet he did such-and-such; so we came to him and found him in the mosque of Banu so-and-so, and we spoke to him, and he came with us until he sat in the gathering he had been in, or near it. Then he said: Praise belongs to Allah; whatever He wills He places before Him and whatever He wills He places behind Him; and among eloquence is magic — then he turned to us and spoke to us, and instructed us and taught us."
"18166","Those named Mujammi'. Mujammi' ibn Jariyah al-Ansari. 1075 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Ibn Shihab narrated to me that he heard Abdullah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Tha'labah al-Ansari narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid al-Ansari — from Banu Amr ibn Awf — who said: I heard my uncle Mujammi' ibn Jariyah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The son of Mary will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd."
"18167","1076 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Tha'labah al-Ansari, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Mujammi' ibn Jariyah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The son of Mary will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd, or beside Ludd."
"18168","1077 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Tha'labah narrated to me that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah say: I heard my uncle Mujammi' ibn Jariyah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and he mentioned the Dajjal, saying: By the One in whose hand is my soul, the son of Mary will surely kill him at the gate of Ludd."
"18169","1078 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Buhlul ibn Hakim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Tha'labah al-Ansari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The son of Mary will kill the false Messiah at the gate of Ludd."
"18170","1079 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Tha'labah al-Ansari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah, from his uncle Mujammi' ibn Jariyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Mary will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd."
"18171","1080 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Tha'labah al-Ansari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah, from his uncle Mujammi' ibn Jariyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Mary will kill the false Messiah at the gate of Ludd."
"18172","1081 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ayli narrated to us, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Ibn Shihab, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Tha'labah al-Ansari narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah al-Ansari, from his uncle Mujammi' ibn Jariyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The son of Mary will kill the false Messiah at the gate of Ludd."
"18173","1082 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, Mujammi' ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, (Ha). And Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Mujammi' ibn Ya'qub narrated to me, from his father who said: I heard my uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his uncle Mujammi' ibn Jariyah say: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Madinah, until when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached Kura' al-Ghamim, people were rushing toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Some people said to others: What is the matter with the people? He said: Revelation has come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So we hastened until we found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing at Kura' al-Ghamim; and when the people gathered he recited to them: (Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory). Some of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, is it a victory? He said: Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, indeed it is a victory. Then it was divided among the people of al-Hudaybiyyah into eighteen shares; the army was fifteen hundred, among them three hundred horsemen, and the horseman received two shares — and the wording is that of the hadith of Ibn al-Tabba'."
"18174","1083 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah, from Ya'qub ibn Mujammi' ibn Jariyah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for the funeral of a man from Banu Amr ibn Awf until he reached the graveyard, and said: Peace be upon the people of the graves — three times — whoever among you were of the believers and the Muslims; you have gone before us and we follow you; may Allah grant us and you well-being."
"18175","1084 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Mujammi' and Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that a man among them called Khidham married his daughter called Khansa' (in marriage), and she disliked him; so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he annulled it. And we used to say that she was previously married."
"18176","1085 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (Ha). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us — both said: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Humran ibn A'yan, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Jariyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him. Ibn Abi Shaybah added in his hadith: So we lined up behind him in two rows."
"18177","1086 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhram narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, that Hisham ibn Yahya informed him that Ikrimah ibn Salamah informed him that two brothers from Banu al-Mughirah met Mujammi' ibn Yazid al-Ansari, and he said: I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that a neighbour not prevent his neighbour from planting a beam in his wall."
"18178","1087 - Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Muqbil narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Hisham ibn Yahya informed him that Ikrimah ibn Salamah ibn Abi Rabi'ah informed him that two brothers from Banu al-Mughirah — one of them swore by emancipation against his fellow that he would not let him place a beam in his wall — met Mujammi' ibn Yazid and men from the Ansar, and they said: We bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A neighbour shall not prevent his neighbour from placing a beam in his wall. So he said: O brother, I knew it was decreed for you against me, so why did you set up pillars apart from my wall? So he set up pillars. Amr said: And I saw those pillars."
"18179","Those named Makhramah. Makhramah ibn Nawfal ibn Uhayb ibn Abd Manaf ibn Zuhrah ibn Kilab ibn Murrah ibn Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy; and his mother was Ruqayqah bint Abi Sufi ibn Hashim ibn Abd Manaf. 1 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Makhramah ibn Nawfal, kunyah Abu al-Miswar, died in the year fifty-four, aged seventy years; and it has been said: when he was one hundred and fifteen years old. He became Muslim on the day of the Conquest, and he was among those whose hearts were to be reconciled."
"18180","What Makhramah ibn Nawfal transmitted. 2 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam and Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, (Ha). And Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from his father who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proclaimed Islam openly, all the people of Makkah became Muslim — and that was before prayer was made obligatory — so much so that when he recited the prostration verse they prostrated, and none of them could prostrate because of the crowding, until the chiefs of Quraysh came: al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah, and Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, and others; and they were at al-Ta'if on their land, and they said: Will you abandon the religion of your forefathers? So they disbelieved."
"18181","Those named Miswar. Miswar ibn Makhramah ibn Nawfal ibn Uhayb al-Zuhri; his mother was the sister of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, it is said her name was Ramlah; and Miswar had Juwayriyah bint Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and she was the mother of his son Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Miswar. 3 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah died on the day the news of the death of Yazid ibn Muawiyah reached Ibn al-Zubayr, in the year sixty-four; Ibn al-Zubayr prayed over him at al-Hajun. He was struck by a catapult stone while praying in the Hijr, and survived five days, dying in Rabi' al-Awwal of the year sixty-four. He was born two years after the Hijrah, and was brought to Madinah at the end of Dhu al-Hijjah in the year eight; he witnessed the year of the Conquest when he was six years old, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when he was eight years old — meaning al-Miswar ibn Makhramah."
"18182","Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah. 4 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Harawi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf al-Ansari narrated to us, Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf informed me, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not walk naked."
"18183","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah. 5 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Hisham ibn Urwah informed me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah lost her husband while she was pregnant, and she remained only a few nights before giving birth; and when she became pure she was proposed to, so she sought the permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to marry when she had given birth, and he permitted her, and she married."
"18184","6 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Miswar, that Subay'ah bint al-Harith lost her husband, and gave birth eight — or seven — (nights) later; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to marry."
"18185","7 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah lost her husband while she was pregnant, and she remained only a few nights before giving birth; and when she recovered from her postpartum bleeding she was proposed to, so she sought the permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to marry when she had given birth, and he permitted her, and she married."
"18186","8 - Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that Subay'ah bint al-Harith al-Aslamiyyah lost her husband while she was pregnant, and she remained only a short while before giving birth; and when she recovered from her postpartum bleeding she was proposed to, so she sought the permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to marry, and he permitted her, and she married."
"18187","9 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah who said: Subay'ah gave birth a few days after her husband's death, and she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought permission to marry, and he permitted her."
"18188","10 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ashkib narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asim ibn Umar, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Subay'ah to marry when she recovered from her postpartum bleeding. Thus said Ibn Ashkib: Asim ibn Umar."
"18189","11 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah lost her husband while she was pregnant, and only a few nights passed before she gave birth; she sought the permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when she recovered from her postpartum bleeding, and he permitted her, and she married."
"18190","12 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from his father Isma'il ibn Ayyash, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to his Companions and said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent me as a mercy to all mankind, so convey on my behalf, may Allah have mercy on you; and do not differ as the disciples differed over Isa (peace be upon him), for he called them to the like of what I call you to: those near in place answered and submitted, and those far in place disliked it. So Isa son of Mary complained of that to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and they awoke with each man among them speaking the tongue of the people to whom he was directed. Then Isa son of Mary (peace be upon him) said to them: This is a matter Allah has decreed for you, so go and do it. So the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We, O Messenger of Allah, will convey on your behalf, so send us wherever you wish. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abdullah ibn Hudhafah to Kisra, and sent Salit ibn Amr to Hawdhah ibn Ali, the ruler of al-Yamamah, and sent al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami to al-Mundhir ibn Sawa, the ruler of Hajar, and sent Amr ibn al-As to Jayfar and Abbad, the two sons of al-Julanda, the two kings of Oman, and sent Dihyah al-Kalbi to Qaysar, and sent Shuja' ibn Wahb al-Asadi to al-Mundhir ibn al-Harith ibn Abi Shimr al-Ghassani, and sent Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri to al-Najashi. They all returned before the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while he was in al-Bahrayn."
"18191","13 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwan ibn al-Hakam, each confirming the other, both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah with somewhat over a thousand of his Companions, until when they were at Dhu al-Hulayfah the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) garlanded the sacrificial animals and marked them, then entered ihram for Umrah. He sent ahead a scout from Khuza'ah to inform him about Quraysh, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marched until, at Ghadir al-Ashtat near Usfan, his Khuza'i scout came to him and said: I left Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy and Amir ibn Lu'ayy, who have gathered the Ahabish against you and gathered troops against you; they will fight you and bar you from the Sacred House. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Advise me: do you think I should incline toward the offspring of those who aided them and strike them — if they sit still, they sit bereaved and despoiled, and if they come, it will be a neck Allah has cut — or do you think we should head for the House, and whoever bars us from it we fight? Abu Bakr said: Allah and His Messenger know best, O Prophet of Allah; we came only as pilgrims, not to fight anyone, but whoever stands between us and the House we will fight. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then proceed. They proceeded until on part of the road the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Khalid ibn al-Walid is at al-Ghamim with horsemen of Quraysh as an advance guard, so take the right side. By Allah, Khalid did not perceive them until the dust of the army appeared to him, so he galloped off as a Warner to Quraysh. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marched until at the pass by which they would descend upon them, his she-camel knelt. The people said: Hal hal; they said: al-Qaswa has balked, al-Qaswa has balked. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Qaswa has not balked, nor is that in her character; rather He who restrained the Elephant has restrained her. Then he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, they will not ask me for any plan by which they honour the sanctities of Allah but I will grant it to them. Then he urged her and she sprang up with him; he turned away from them until he halted at the farthest part of al-Hudaybiyyah at a scant-water well which people were scooping sparingly; the people soon drained it, and complained of thirst to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he pulled an arrow from his quiver and ordered them to place it in it. He said: By Allah, it kept gushing with fresh water for them until they departed from it. While they were thus, Budayl ibn Warqa al-Khuza'i came to them with men of his people from Khuza'ah — and they were the trusted confidants of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the people of Tihamah — and said: I left Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy and Amir ibn Lu'ayy camped at the wells of al-Hudaybiyyah, with the milking she-camels with their young, and they will fight you and bar you from the House. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We did not come to fight anyone, but we came as pilgrims; Quraysh have been exhausted by war and harmed by it. If they wish, I will grant them a truce and they leave me with the people: if I prevail, they may enter into what the people entered if they wish, otherwise they will have rested; and if they refuse, by the One in whose hand is my soul, I will fight them over this matter of mine until my neck is severed or Allah carries out His command. Budayl said: I will convey to them what you say. He went until he came to Quraysh and said: We have come to you from this man, and we heard him say something; if you wish we will present it to you. Their fools said: We have no need for you to tell us anything about him; and their men of judgement said: Bring what you heard him say. He said: I heard him say such-and-such, and he told them what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said. Then Urwah ibn Mas'ud al-Thaqafi stood and said: O people, am I not as a son to you? They said: Yes. He said: Am I not as a father to you? They said: Yes. He said: Do you suspect me? They said: No. He said: Do you not know that I summoned the people of Ukaz, and when they held back from me I came to you with my family and children and those who obeyed me? They said: Yes. He said: He has offered you a sound plan, so accept it and let me go to him. They said: Go to him. So he came to him and began speaking to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him something like what he had said to Budayl. At that Urwah said: O Muhammad, tell me: if you exterminate your people, have you heard of any Arab before you who uprooted his kin? And if the other outcome occurs, by Allah I see faces and a rabble of people likely to flee and leave you. So Abu Bakr said: Suck the clitoris of al-Lat; shall we flee and leave him? He said: Who is this? He said: Abu Bakr. He said: But for a favour you did me which I have not yet repaid I would have answered you. He said: And he kept speaking to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and each time he spoke he took hold of his beard, while al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah stood over the head of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in helmet with his sword; each time Urwah reached his hand toward the beard of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he struck his hand with the shoe of the sword, saying: Keep your hand off the beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Urwah raised his head and said: Who is this? He said: This is al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. He said: O treacherous one, am I not striving to settle your treachery? Now al-Mughirah had accompanied some people in the Jahiliyyah and killed them and taken their wealth, then come and become Muslim; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for Islam I accept, but as for the wealth I have nothing to do with it. Then Urwah began eyeing the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never spat out mucus but it fell into the hand of one of them, and he rubbed his face and skin with it; when he commanded they hastened to his command; when he performed wudu they almost fought over his wudu water; when they spoke they lowered their voices before him, and they did not gaze sharply at him out of reverence for him. So Urwah returned to his fellows and said: O people, by Allah I have come as a delegate to kings — I came to Qaysar and Kisra and al-Najashi — and by Allah I never saw any king honoured by his companions as the companions of Muhammad honour Muhammad. By Allah, he never spat out mucus but it fell into the palm of one of them and he rubbed his face and skin with it; when he commanded them they hastened to his command; when he performed wudu they almost fought over his wudu water; when they spoke they lowered their voices before him, and they did not gaze sharply at him out of reverence for him; and he has offered you a sound plan, so accept it. Then a man of Banu Kinanah said: Let me go to him. They said: Go to him. When he appeared before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is so-and-so, and he is of a people who honour the sacrificial camels, so drive them forward for him. So they were driven forward for him, and the people met him chanting the talbiyah. When he saw that he said: Glory be to Allah, these people should not be barred from the House. He said: When he returned to his fellows he said: I saw the sacrificial camels garlanded and marked; I do not think they should be barred from the House. Then a man among them called Mikraz ibn Hafs said: Let me go to him. They said: Go to him. When he appeared before them, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is Mikraz ibn Hafs, and he is a wicked man. He began speaking to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and while he was speaking, Suhayl ibn Amr came. He said: Come, write a document between us and you. He summoned the scribe, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Suhayl said: As for al-Rahman, by Allah I do not know what it is; rather write: In Your name, O Allah, as you used to write. The Muslims said: By Allah, he shall write nothing but: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Write: In Your name, O Allah. Then he said: This is what Muhammad the Messenger of Allah has agreed upon. Suhayl said: By Allah, had we known you are the Messenger of Allah we would not have barred you from the House nor fought you; rather write: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, I am indeed the Messenger of Allah though you deny me; write: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On condition that you leave us with the House so we may circumambulate it. Suhayl said: By Allah, the Arabs shall not say we were taken under duress; rather (you may) next year. So he wrote. Then Suhayl said: And on condition that no man of ours comes to you, even if upon your religion, but you return him to us. The Muslims said: Glory be to Allah, how is one returned to the polytheists when he has come as a Muslim? While they were thus, Abu Jandal ibn Suhayl ibn Amr came dragging his fetters, having escaped from the lower part of Makkah until he threw himself among the Muslims. Suhayl said: This, O Muhammad, is the first I settle with you: that you return him to me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have not yet concluded the document. He said: By Allah, then I will never make peace with you over anything. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then grant him to me. He said: I will not grant him to you. He said: Yes, do. He said: I will not do it. Mikraz said: Yes, we have granted him to you. Then Abu Jandal said: O company of Muslims, shall I be returned to the polytheists when I have come as a Muslim? Do you not see what I have suffered? — and he had been tormented severely for Allah's sake. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab said: By Allah, I never doubted since I became Muslim except that day. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Are you not the Prophet of Allah in truth? He said: Yes. I said: Are we not upon the truth and our enemy upon falsehood? He said: Yes. I said: Then why do we concede humiliation in our religion? He said: I am indeed the Messenger of Allah, and I do not disobey Him, and He will aid me. I said: Did you not tell us that we would come to the House and circumambulate it? He said: Yes; did I tell you that you would come to it this year? I said: No. He said: Then you will come to it and circumambulate it. He said: Then I went to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, is this not the Prophet of Allah in truth? He said: Yes. I said: Are we not upon the truth and our enemy upon falsehood? He said: Yes. I said: Then why do we concede humiliation in our religion? He said: O man, he is the Messenger of Allah, and he does not disobey his Lord, and He will aid him; so hold fast to his stirrup until you die, for by Allah he is upon the truth. I said: Did he not tell us that we would come to the House and circumambulate it? He said: Yes; did he tell you that you would come to it this year? I said: No. He said: Then you will come to it and circumambulate it. When he finished settling the document, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Stand, slaughter, then shave. He said: By Allah, not one man among them stood until he said it three times. When none of them stood, he stood and entered upon Umm Salamah, and told her what he had met from the people. Umm Salamah said: O Prophet of Allah, do you want that? Go out, then speak to none of them a word until you slaughter your sacrificial animal and summon your barber to shave you. So he stood and went out and spoke to none of them until he did that: he slaughtered his animal and summoned his barber who shaved him. When they saw that, they stood and slaughtered, and some began shaving others until some almost killed others out of grief. Then believing women came as emigrants, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: (O you who believe, when the believing women come to you as emigrants) until (the bonds of the disbelieving women). So Umar divorced that day two wives he had in polytheism; one of them Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan married, and the other Safwan ibn Umayyah married. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to Madinah, and Abu Basir came to him — a man of Quraysh — and he was a Muslim; so they sent two men seeking him, saying: (Honour) the covenant you made for us. So he handed him over to the two men. They went out until at Dhu al-Hulayfah they alighted eating dates of theirs. Abu Basir said to one of the two men: By Allah, I see this sword of yours, O so-and-so, is fine. The other drew it and said: Yes, by Allah it is fine; I have tried it and tried it. Abu Basir said: Show me, let me look at it. So he let him have it, and he struck him with it until he grew cold (died), and the other fled until he reached Madinah and entered the mosque running. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he saw him: This man has seen terror. When he reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: By Allah, my companion has been killed, and I am to be killed. Then Abu Basir came and said: O Prophet of Allah, by Allah, Allah has fulfilled your covenant: you returned me to them, then Allah delivered me from them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to his mother, a kindler of war, had he men with him. When he heard that he knew he would return him to them, so he went out until he reached the seashore. He said: And Abu Jandal ibn Suhayl escaped from them and joined Abu Basir; and no Muslim man of Quraysh went out but joined Abu Basir, until a band gathered among them. He said: By Allah, they never heard of a camel caravan of Quraysh going out to al-Sham but they waylaid it, killed them and took their wealth. So Quraysh sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), beseeching him by Allah and kinship to send to them: whoever comes to him is safe. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent word, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: (And He it is who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them in the valley of Makkah) until (the pride of the Jahiliyyah). And the pride of Quraysh was that they did not affirm that he is the Prophet of Allah, nor affirmed In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, and they stood between him and the House."
"18192","14 - Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwan ibn al-Hakam, that both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the year of al-Hudaybiyyah intending to visit the House, not intending fighting; and he drove with him seventy sacrificial camels. The people were seven hundred men, each camel on behalf of ten persons. Ibn Ishaq said: Jabir ibn Abd Allah said: We, the people of al-Hudaybiyyah, were fourteen hundred. Al-Zuhri said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out until at Usfan he was met by Bishr ibn Sufyan al-Ka'bi, who said to him: O Messenger of Allah, these Quraysh bar your way; they have come out with the milking she-camels with their young, until it was said: They have donned leopard skins, camped at Dhu Tuwa, pledging to Allah that you shall never enter it upon them; and this Khalid ibn al-Walid is among their troops, and they have sent him ahead to Kura' al-Ghamim. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to Quraysh; war has consumed them. What would it harm them to leave me with the rest of the Arabs? If they strike me, that is what they wanted; and if Allah grants me victory over them, they would enter Islam in full numbers; and if they do not, they would fight with strength in them. What does Quraysh think? By Allah, I will keep striving against them over that with which Allah sent me until Allah grants me victory or this neck-vein is severed. Then he said: Who will take us out by a route other than their route? — and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ma'mar from al-Zuhri."
"18193","15 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, the nephew of al-Zuhri narrated to us, from his uncle, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that he heard al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwan ibn al-Hakam reporting of the report of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the campaign of al-Hudaybiyyah. Among what Urwah informed me from them was that they said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Suhayl ibn Amr on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah concerning the settlement of the truce period, among what Suhayl ibn Amr stipulated upon him was his saying: No one of ours shall come to you, even if upon your religion, but you return him to us and leave him between us and him. Suhayl refused to settle with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except on that; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned Abu Jandal ibn Suhayl that day to his father Suhayl ibn Amr; no man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but he returned him during that period, even if a Muslim. Then believing women came as emigrants — and Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt — then she went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), being of marriageable age; her family came asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to return her to them, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning the believing women what He revealed."
"18194","16 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwan who said: Surat al-Fath was revealed between Makkah and Madinah concerning al-Hudaybiyyah, from its beginning to its end."
"18195","17 - Abdan ibn Abd al-Samad Maghammah narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he divided Khaybar, divided it into eighty shares; the men were eighteen hundred, the horses two hundred; four hundred shares for the horsemen: each share on behalf of eighteen hundred shares(?); every hundred shares had a chief: Umar ibn al-Khattab was a chief, Ali was a chief, Talhah was a chief, al-Zubayr was a chief, Asim ibn Adi was a chief; and the share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with Asim ibn Adi."
"18196","Ali ibn al-Husayn, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah. 18 - Abu Usamah Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani' al-Rusafi narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, Ali ibn al-Husayn informed me that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him that Ali ibn Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl while Fatimah bint Rasulillah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with him. When Fatimah heard of that she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: Your people say that you do not grow angry for your daughters, and this Ali is marrying the daughter of Abu Jahl. Al-Miswar said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood upon the minbar, and I heard him testify (tashahhud) then say: To proceed: I married Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi' and he spoke to me and told me the truth; and Fatimah bint Muhammad is a piece of me, and I dislike that you tempt her; and by Allah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the daughter of the enemy of Allah will never be joined with one man ever. He said: So Ali abandoned the proposal."
"18197","19 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us, from al-Zuhri, Ali ibn al-Husayn informed me that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him that Ali ibn Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl; he mentioned the hadith."
"18198","20 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Walid ibn Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah al-Du'ali who informed him that Ibn Shihab narrated to him that Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to him that when he arrived in Madinah from Yazid ibn Muawiyah — at the killing of al-Husayn ibn Ali — al-Miswar ibn Makhramah met him and said to him: Have you any need you would command me with? I said: No. He said: Will you give me the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? For I fear the people will overpower you for it; and by Allah, if you give it to me none shall reach it ever until my soul is spent for it. Ali ibn Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl over Fatimah, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing the people concerning that upon this minbar of his — and I was that day adolescent — saying: Fatimah is from me, and I fear she will be tempted in her religion. Then he mentioned the in-law of Banu Abd Shams and praised Abu al-As for his kinship by marriage to him, saying: He spoke to me truthfully and promised me and fulfilled to me; and I do not forbid a lawful thing nor permit an unlawful thing, but by Allah the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the daughter of the enemy of Allah will never be joined."
"18199","21 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father informed us, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Rashid narrating, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that Ali ibn Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl and pledged the marriage; so Fatimah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your people say that you do not grow angry for your daughters, and Ali has proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Fatimah is but a piece of me, and I dislike that she be tempted. And he mentioned Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi' and praised him well, saying: The daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the daughter of the enemy of Allah are not joined."
"18200","Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah. 22 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, the nephew of al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall pray while feeling any discomfort — meaning stool and urine."
"18201","Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah. 23 - Abdan ibn Ahmad and Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Dimashqi narrated to us, they said: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The infant does not inherit until he cries out at birth; his crying out is that he shouts or weeps or sneezes."
"18202","Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Tufayl, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah. 24 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Awf ibn al-Harith — and he is the son of A'ishah's maternal sister — that A'ishah narrated to him that Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr said, concerning a sale or gift A'ishah had given: By Allah, A'ishah shall desist or I shall place her under interdiction. A'ishah said: Did he say this? They said: Yes. So A'ishah said: It is a vow upon me to Allah never to speak a word to Ibn al-Zubayr ever. Then Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr sought intercession to her when her forsaking him grew long, and A'ishah said: By Allah, I will not let anyone intercede for him, nor will I ever break the vow I vowed. When that grew long upon Ibn al-Zubayr he spoke to al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth — both of Zuhrah — and said to them: I ask you by Allah but to admit me to A'ishah, for it is not lawful for her to vow to sever me. So al-Miswar and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad came with Ibn al-Zubayr wrapped over him in their cloaks until they sought permission of A'ishah, saying: Peace be upon the Prophet and the mercy of Allah; may we enter? A'ishah said: Enter. They said: All of us, O Mother of the Believers? She said: Enter, all of you — while A'ishah did not know that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr rushed through the veil and embraced A'ishah, entreating her and weeping; and al-Miswar and Abd al-Rahman entreated A'ishah to speak to him and accept from him, saying to her: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade what you know of forsaking, for it is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three nights. When they pressed A'ishah with reminding and warning, she began reminding them and weeping, saying: I have vowed, and the vow is grave. They kept at her until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr, and she freed forty slaves for her vow; then she would remember that vow of hers after she had freed forty slaves, and weep until her tears wet her head-cover."
"18203","25 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Awf ibn al-Harith ibn Tufayl — and he is the son of A'ishah's maternal sister, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — that A'ishah narrated to him that Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr said, concerning a sale or gift A'ishah had given: By Allah, A'ishah shall desist or I shall place her under interdiction. She said: Did he say this? They said: Yes. A'ishah said: Then it is a vow to Allah never to speak a word to Ibn al-Zubayr ever. Then Ibn al-Zubayr sought intercession to her when her forsaking him grew long, and she said: By Allah, I will never let anyone intercede for him, nor break the vow I vowed ever. When that grew long upon Ibn al-Zubayr he spoke to al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth — both of Banu Zuhrah — and said to them: I ask you by Allah but to admit me to A'ishah, for it is not lawful for her to vow to sever me. So al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad came with him wrapped over him in their cloaks until they sought permission of A'ishah, saying: Peace be upon the Prophet and the mercy of Allah; may we enter? A'ishah said: Enter. They said: All of us, O Mother of the Believers? She said: Yes, enter, all of you — while A'ishah did not know that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr entered through the veil and embraced A'ishah, entreating her and weeping; and al-Miswar and Abd al-Rahman entreated A'ishah to speak to him and accept from him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade what you know of forsaking, for it is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three nights. When they pressed A'ishah with reminding and warning, she began reminding them and weeping, saying: I have vowed, and the vow is grave. They kept at her until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr, and she freed forty slaves for her vow; then she would remember that vow of hers after she had freed forty slaves, and weep until her tears wet her head-cover."
"18204","26 - Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-San'ani narrated to us, (Ha). And Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Mahmud ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Kathir al-Qari narrated to us, both said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri narrated to me, Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Tufayl al-Azdi — Azd Shanu'ah, and he is the son of A'ishah's maternal sister — informed me that A'ishah was told that Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr had said, concerning a house of hers she had sold, and Abdullah disapproved of the sale of that house, saying: By Allah, A'ishah shall desist from selling her properties or I shall place her under interdiction. A'ishah said: Did he say that? They said: He said that. She said: It is upon me to Allah never to speak to him until death parts me and him — and he mentioned the hadith."
"18205","27 - Abu Usamah Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani' al-Rusafi narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Tufayl narrated to me — and he is the son of A'ishah's maternal sister, may Allah be pleased with her, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — that A'ishah was told that Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr had said, concerning a sale or gifts A'ishah had given: By Allah, A'ishah shall desist or I shall place her under interdiction. She said: Did he say this? They said: Yes. She said: It is a vow upon me to Allah never to speak a word to Ibn al-Zubayr ever. Then Ibn al-Zubayr sought the intercession of people to her when she prolonged forsaking him, and she said: By Allah, I will not let anyone intercede for him, nor break my vow ever. When that grew long upon Ibn al-Zubayr he spoke to al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth — both of Banu Zuhrah — and said to them: I ask you by Allah but to admit me to A'ishah, for it is not lawful for her to vow to sever me. So al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth came wrapped over him in their cloaks until they sought permission of A'ishah, saying: Peace be upon the Prophet and the mercy and blessings of Allah; may we enter? A'ishah said: Enter. They said: All of us, O Mother of the Believers? She said: Yes, enter, all of you — while A'ishah did not perceive that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr entered through the veil and embraced A'ishah, entreating her and weeping; and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad entreated A'ishah by Allah to speak to him and accept from him, saying to her: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade forsaking as you know, saying: It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three nights. When they pressed A'ishah with reminding and warning, she began reminding them and weeping, saying: I have vowed, and the vow is grave indeed. They kept at her until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr, then freed forty slaves for her vow; then she would remember that vow of hers after she had freed forty slaves, then weep until her tears wet her head-cover."
"18206","Muhammad ibn Qays, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah. 28 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at Arafat, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed: the people of shirk and idols used to depart from this place when the sun was over the mountain-tops as if turbans of men upon their faces; and we depart after it has set. And they used to depart from al-Mash'ar al-Haram when the sun was spread out."
"18207","Qays ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Makhramah, from al-Miswar. 29 - Musa ibn Harun and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Qays ibn Makhramah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"18208","Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah. 30 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Sa'id, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Umm Bakr bint al-Miswar, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that Hasan ibn Hasan sent to al-Miswar seeking a daughter of his in marriage. He said: Tell him to meet me at a time he mentioned. He met him, and al-Miswar praised Allah and said: There is no kinship, nor lineage, nor marriage tie dearer to me than your kinship and marriage tie; but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fatimah is a branch of me; what delights her delights me, and what grieves her grieves me; and on the Day of Resurrection lineages are cut off except my lineage and my cause. And beneath you (in marriage) is her daughter; were I to marry you to her, that would grieve her. So he left, excusing him."
"18209","Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah. 31 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Daqiqi narrated to us, Imran ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever takes anything of land will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."
"18210","Umm Bakr bint al-Miswar, from her father. 32 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, al-Nu'man ibn Shibl al-Bahili narrated to us, (Ha). And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, he said: My aunt Umm Bakr bint al-Miswar ibn Makhramah narrated to me, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah who said: A Jew passed by me while I was behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was performing wudu; he pushed his garment off his back, and there was the Seal of Prophethood on his back. The Jew said: Lift his garment off his back. So I went to lift the garment of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) off his back, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) splashed a handful of water in my face."
"18211","33 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya al-Abdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, my aunt Umm Bakr bint al-Miswar ibn Makhramah narrated to me that al-Hasan ibn Ali proposed to al-Miswar ibn Makhramah for his daughter, and he married her to him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every cause and lineage is cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my cause and my lineage."
"18212","Miswar ibn Yazid al-Asadi, then al-Kahili. 34 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (Ha). And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, (Ha). And Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ali ibn Ma'bad al-Raqqi narrated to us, they said: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Kahili narrated to us, from Miswar ibn Yazid who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in prayer, and he left something he did not recite. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, it is such-and-such. He said: Why did you not remind me of it? He said: I thought it had been abrogated."
"18213","The remainder of the letter Mim. Those named Mu'adh. Mu'adh ibn Jabal al-Ansari, Aqabi, Badri, kunyah Abu Abd al-Rahman. Mention of the expeditions of Mu'adh, his age, his death, and of his reports. 35 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed al-Aqabah, then from Banu Salimah: Mu'adh ibn Jabal ibn Amr ibn A'idh ibn Adi ibn Ka'b ibn Uddiyy ibn Sa'd ibn Adi ibn Asad ibn Saridah ibn Tazid ibn Jusham; and he witnessed Badr."
"18214","36 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Mu'adh ibn Jabal."
"18215","37 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal ibn Amr ibn Aws ibn A'idh ibn Adi ibn Ka'b ibn Uddiyy witnessed Badr and al-Aqabah. Ibn Ishaq said: Banu Salimah claimed him only because he was the maternal brother of Suhayl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Jadd ibn Qays ibn Sakhr ibn Khansa ibn Sinan ibn Ubayd ibn Adi ibn Ghanm ibn Ka'b ibn Salamah."
"18216","38 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old; and whoever raises his age says: thirty-two years."
"18217","39 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old; and whoever raises his age says: thirty-two years."
"18218","40 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik ibn Anas say: Mu'adh ibn Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old, though one says: thirty-two; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal will be ahead of the scholars by a rank on the Day of Resurrection. Ibn Bukayr said: And al-ratwah means: the station."
"18219","41 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Azhar al-Ansari, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal will be ahead of the scholars by a rank."
"18220","42 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal died when he was thirty-three or thirty-four years old."
"18221","43 - Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal died in the plague of Amwas in the year seventeen or eighteen."
"18222","44 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal was a handsome, generous youth, among the best youths of his people; he was never asked for anything but he gave it, until he incurred a debt that consumed his wealth. He said: So he spoke to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to speak to his creditors, and he did. They remitted nothing for him; had anyone been spared by anyone's word, Mu'adh would have been spared by the word of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) summoned him and did not leave until he sold his property and divided it among his creditors; then Mu'adh stood with no wealth. When he performed Hajj, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Yemen to restore him. He said: And the first to trade with this wealth was Mu'adh; he came to Abu Bakr from Yemen after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had died."
"18223","45 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated to us, he said: I came to Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, and he brought out to me a sheet; in it was: From Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and Mu'adh ibn Jabal to Umar ibn al-Khattab: Peace be upon you; to proceed: we knew you when your own affair was your concern, and now you have been put in charge of the affair of this ummah, its red and its black. The lowly and the noble sit before you, and the enemy and the friend, and each has his share of justice; so consider how you will be at that, O Umar. For we warn you of a day when faces will be humbled, hearts will dry up, and proofs will be cut off before the proof of a King who has subdued them by His might; and creation will be submissive to Him, hoping for His mercy and fearing His punishment. And we used to say that the affair of this ummah at the end of its time will return to their being brothers in public and enemies in secret; and we seek refuge with Allah lest our letter descend to other than the place it left in our hearts, for we wrote it only as counsel to you. Peace be upon you. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to them: From Umar ibn al-Khattab to Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with them both: Peace be upon you both; to proceed: your letter reached me, mentioning that you knew me when my own affair was my concern, and now I have been put in charge of the affair of this ummah, its red and its black; the noble and the lowly, the enemy and the friend sit before me, and each has a share of justice. You wrote: How will you be at that, O Umar; and they have no strength nor power at that except through Allah. You wrote warning me of what the nations before us were warned of of old; and the alternation of night and day through people's lifespans brings every distant thing near, and brings every new thing, and brings every promised thing, until people arrive at their abodes in Paradise and Hell. You wrote warning me that the affair of this ummah will return at the end of its time to their being brothers in public and enemies in secret; but you are not of those, nor is this the time of that. That is a time when desire and fear will appear: some people's desire for others will be for the soundness of their worldly life. You wrote seeking refuge with Allah lest I place your letter to other than the place it left in your hearts, and that you wrote it as counsel to me; and you spoke truly. So do not cease writing to me, for I cannot do without you. Peace be upon you both."
"18224","46 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif informed us, Abu Hazim informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'id ibn Yarbu', from Malik al-Dar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab took four hundred dinars and placed them in a purse, saying to a servant: Go with them to Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, then linger a while in the house to see what he does. The servant went with them to him, saying: The Commander of the Believers says to you: Use this for some of your need. He said: May Allah join him and have mercy on him. Then he said: Come, O slave-girl, take these seven to so-and-so, and these five to so-and-so, until he spent them all. The servant returned and told him; and he found he had prepared the like for Mu'adh ibn Jabal, saying: Go with this to Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and linger in the house to see what he does. He went with them to him, saying: The Commander of the Believers says to you: Use this for some of your need. He said — may Allah have mercy on him and join him — : Come, O slave-girl, go to the house of so-and-so with such-and-such, and go to the house of so-and-so with such-and-such. Then the wife of Mu'adh looked out and said: By Allah, we are poor, so give us; and only two dinars remained in the rag, so he pushed them to her. The servant returned to Umar and told him, and he rejoiced at that, saying: They are brothers, one of the other."
"18225","47 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu al-Ahwas and others, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal was a nation (ummah), devout to Allah, upright, and was not of the polytheists. One of his companions said to him: (That was) Ibrahim. He said: I have not forgotten. Then he said: Do you know what an ummah is? They said: No. He said: One who teaches people good. He said: Do you know what devout (qanit) is? They said: No. He said: Obedient to Allah."
"18226","48 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: I heard Awn ibn Bakr al-Rasibi narrating, from Thawr ibn Yazid who said: When Mu'adh would rise for tahajjud at night he would say: O Allah, eyes have slept and stars have set, while You are the Living, the Sustainer. O Allah, my seeking Paradise is slow and my fleeing from the Fire is weak. O Allah, grant me with You guidance You will return to me on the Day of Resurrection; indeed You do not break the promise."
"18227","49 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la al-San'ani narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin who said: A man came to Mu'adh ibn Jabal, with his companions greeting him and bidding him farewell, and he said: I counsel you with two matters: if you guard them you will be guarded. You cannot do without your share of this world, yet you are poorer toward your share of the Hereafter. So prefer your share of the Hereafter over your share of this world until you order it for yourself in order, and it departs with you wherever you depart."
"18228","50 - Sahl ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that Mu'adh ibn Jabal fainted, and his sister began saying: O my mountain — or another word. When he recovered he said: You kept harming me all today. She said: It would grieve me to harm you. He said: An angel, stern in rebuke, kept saying whenever you said: O such-and-such: Are you so? And I would say: No."
"18229","51 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Malik ibn Yakhamir who said: I saw Mu'adh ibn Jabal killing lice and fleas in the mosque."
"18230","What Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah transmitted from Mu'adh. 52 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ziyad ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn al-Harith, from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two men love one another for Allah but Allah places for them a seat, and they are seated upon it until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, finishes the Reckoning. So Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: Abu Ubaydah spoke the truth."
"18231","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Mu'adh. 53 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, they said: Shadh ibn al-Fayyad narrated to us, Abu Qahdham narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abdullah ibn Umar who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal passed by weeping. He said: What makes you weep? He said: A hadith I heard from the occupant of this grave — meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — : The least of showing off is shirk; and the most beloved servants to Allah are the God-fearing, the hidden, who when absent are not missed, and when present are not known; those are the leaders of guidance and the lamps of knowledge."
"18232","Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from Mu'adh. 54 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Ya'qub, from Qays ibn Rafi', from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that he passed by Mu'adh ibn Jabal while he stood at his door, gesturing with his hand as if speaking to himself. Abdullah said to him: What is the matter with you, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, speaking to yourself? He said: What is it to the enemy of Allah — meaning — that he distract me from what I heard from Muhammad the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said to me: You now strive through your time in your house, not going out to the gathering; for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever strives in the path of Allah is guaranteed by Allah, Mighty and Majestic; and whoever visits a sick person is guaranteed by Allah, Mighty and Majestic; and whoever goes to the mosque morning or evening is guaranteed by Allah; and whoever sits in his house without backbiting anyone with evil is guaranteed by Allah. So the enemy of Allah wants to draw me out of my house to the gathering."
"18233","55 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, (Ha). And Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tariq narrated to us, (Ha). And Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Ulayy ibn Rabah, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five acts — whoever does one of them is guaranteed by Allah: whoever visits a sick person, or goes out with a funeral, or goes out as a warrior, or enters upon his ruler intending to honour and revere him, or sits in his house so people are safe from him and he is safe from people."
"18234","56 - al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Mansur ibn Ammar narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (Ha). And Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hibban al-Raqqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Bukayr ibn Bakkar al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Mujashi' ibn Amr narrated to us, both said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As narrated to me that Mu'adh ibn Jabal informed him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us changed in colour and said: I am Muhammad; I have been given the openings of speech and its sealings, so obey me while I am among you; and when I am taken away, upon you is the Book of Allah: permit its lawful and forbid its unlawful. Death has come to you; it comes with spirit and rest — a decree from Allah that preceded. Trials have come to you like pieces of the dark night; whenever one generation of messengers goes, another comes. Prophethood has been succeeded and become kingship. May Allah have mercy on whoever takes it by its right and leaves it as he entered it. Hold, O Mu'adh, and count. He said: When I reached five, he said: Yazid; may Allah not bless Yazid. Then his eyes shed tears and he said: Husayn has been announced dead to me; his soil was brought to me, and his killer named to me. By the One in whose hand is my soul, he will not be killed among a people who do not defend him but Allah will set their hearts and breasts at variance, impose their worst upon them, and clothe them in factions. Then he said: Alas for the fledglings of the household of Muhammad from a succeeding, appointed, luxurious caliph who will kill my successor and the successor of the successor. Hold, O Mu'adh. When I reached ten he said: al-Walid — the name of Pharaoh, destroyer of the ordinances of Islam; before him a man of his household; Allah will surely unsheathe His sword, and it has no sheath; and people will differ and become thus — and he interlaced his fingers. Then he said: After one hundred and twenty, swift death and abundant killing; therein is their ruin; and there will rule over them a man of the progeny of al-Abbas — and the wording of both is one."
"18235","57 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they mentioned a man before him, saying: How incapable he is. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have backbitten your brother. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we said what is in him. He said: If you said what is not in him, you have slandered him."
"18236","58 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Imran narrated to me that Abu al-Simt Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Mahri narrated to him, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that Mu'adh ibn Jabal intended a journey and said: O Messenger of Allah, counsel me. He said: Worship Allah and associate nothing with Him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, give me more. He said: And when you do wrong, do good. He said: O Messenger of Allah, give me more. He said: Be upright, and improve your character."
"18237","Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal. 59 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar, Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal said in the illness in which he died: Were it not that you would rely (upon it), I would narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever dies with La ilaha illa Allah certain in his heart enters Paradise."
"18238","60 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar who said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: Mu'adh ibn Jabal said while ill: Uncover from me the enclosure of the tent that I may narrate to you a hadith — were it not for my state I would not narrate it to you — I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies saying La ilaha illa Allah with certainty from himself enters Paradise."
"18239","61 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both said: Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, Hatim ibn Abi Saghairah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: When Mu'adh ibn Jabal was attended (by death) he said: Lift from me the curtain of the tent, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies worshipping Allah, associating nothing with Him, enters Paradise."
"18240","62 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Talhah ibn Amr narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari informed him that he attended Mu'adh ibn Jabal when death came to him, and Mu'adh said: Uncover from me the curtain of the tent; were it not for what has befallen me from Allah I would not have told you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger enters Paradise."
"18241","63 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: One who witnessed Mu'adh ibn Jabal when death came to him informed us, saying: Lift from me the curtain of the tent that I may narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — nothing prevented me from narrating it to you but that you would rely upon it — I heard him say: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah sincerely from his heart enters Paradise, and the Fire will not touch him."
"18242","64 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Silah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ata informed me, from Jabir, Mu'adh informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever grants a man security then kills him, the Fire is due for him, even if the slain one was a disbeliever."
"18243","Abdullah ibn Qays Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal. 65 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, (Ha). And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Khalid, Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to me, Abu Burdah narrated to us, from Abu Musa who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two men of the Ash'ar — one on my right and the other on my left — while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was using the siwak. Both asked for office. He said: O Abu Musa — or O Abdullah. I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they did not inform me of what was in their minds, nor did I know they sought office; it is as if I look at his siwak beneath his lip. He said to me: We do not appoint over our affair one who seeks it; but go, you, O Abu Musa — or O Abdullah ibn Qays — so he sent him over Yemen, then followed him with Mu'adh ibn Jabal. When he arrived to him he cast a cushion for him, saying: Alight. And there was a bound man. He said: What is this? He said: He was a Jew, then became Muslim, then returned to his evil religion. He said: I will not sit until he is killed — the decree of Allah and His Messenger — three times. So he ordered him and he was killed."
"18244","66 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Burdah narrated to us, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and Mu'adh ibn Jabal to Yemen, ordering them to teach the people the Qur'an. Mu'adh came to Abu Musa visiting him, and there was with him a man bound in iron. He said: O brother, were we sent to torment people, or were we sent to teach them and command them what benefits them? He said to him: He became Muslim, then disbelieved. He said: By the One who sent Muhammad with the truth, I will not move until you burn him with fire. Abu Musa said: We still have something (to settle) with him. Mu'adh said: By Allah, I will never move. He said: So firewood was brought, fire kindled in it, and he cast him (in it)."
"18245","67 - Ahmad ibn Sahl Abu Ghassan al-Askari al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Ma'mar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Amir narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that a man became Muslim then Judaized; Mu'adh came to him while he was with Abu Musa, saying to him: What is this? He said: He became Muslim then Judaized. He said: I will not sit until you kill him — the decree of Allah and His Messenger."
"18246","Ka'b ibn Malik al-Ansari, from Mu'adh. 68 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, both said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib and Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Ibn Shihab."
"18247","Abu Waqid al-Laythi, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal. 69 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, (Ha). And Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, both said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, that Busr ibn Sa'id narrated to him that Abu Waqid al-Laythi said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while we sat upon a mat: There will be tribulation. They said: What shall we do? He said: He returned his hand to the mat and grasped it, saying: They will do thus. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned to them: There will be tribulation — and many people did not hear him. So Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: Do you not hear what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says? They said: What did he say? He said: He says: There will be tribulation. They said: What of us, O Messenger of Allah, and what shall we do? He said: You will return to your first affair."
"18248","al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, from Mu'adh. 70 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he prayed; when he finished his prayer I said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw you do what I never saw you do in prayer. He said: It was a prayer of hope and fear: I asked Allah in it for three things; He granted me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to impose upon my ummah an enemy from other than them who would uproot them, and He granted it to me; and I asked Him not to send upon them a year (of famine) that would destroy them, and He granted it to me; and I asked Him not to make their violence among themselves, and He withheld it from me."
"18249","Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal. 71 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub and al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, (Ha). And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hissan ibn Kahil who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah narrating, from Mu'adh, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No servant dies bearing witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, that returning to a certain heart, but he enters Paradise. It was said to him: Did you hear this from Mu'adh? He said: I heard this from Mu'adh narrating it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"18250","72 - And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hissban ibn Kahil who said: I entered the congregational mosque at al-Basrah and sat beside a white-haired, white-bearded shaykh, and he said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: No soul dies bearing witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, that returning to a believing heart, but Allah forgives him. I said: Did you hear this from Mu'adh ibn Jabal? The people seemed to rebuke him, so he said: Do not rebuke him nor blame him; leave him. I heard that from Mu'adh ibn Jabal reporting it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said to the people: Who is this? They said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah."
"18251","73 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hissban ibn Kahil al-Adawi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like."
"18252","74 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hissban ibn al-Kahil — whose father was a soothsayer in the Jahiliyyah — who said: I entered the mosque during the rule of Uthman, and there was a white-haired, white-bearded shaykh narrating from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he mentioned the like."
"18253","Anas ibn Malik, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal. 75 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Awdh Allah narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out with Mu'adh ibn Jabal at the door; when he saw him he said: O Mu'adh. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Whoever dies associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise. So Mu'adh said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not inform the people? He said: Leave them to compete in deeds, for I fear they will rely upon it."
"18254","76 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise. So Mu'adh said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not give the people glad tidings? He said: I fear they will rely (upon it)."
"18255","77 - Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, the companion of al-Harawi, narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I heard him say: Mu'adh was the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to him: Give the people glad tidings that whoever dies associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise."
"18256","78 - Bakr ibn Muqbil narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Attab, the freedman of Hurmuz — a man of Wasit — from Anas ibn Malik who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hand of mine upon hearing and obeying as much as I could; and I heard him narrating that Mu'adh ibn Jabal was the riding companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Give the people glad tidings that whoever dies associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise. So Mu'adh said: I fear they will rely upon it."
"18257","79 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, sincerely from his heart, enters Paradise."
"18258","80 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Salamah ibn Wardan narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that he heard him say: Mu'adh ibn Jabal came to me and I said: From where have you come, O Mu'adh? He said: I have come from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: What did he say to you? He said: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah sincerely enters Paradise. I said: Shall I go and ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Go. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, Mu'adh ibn Jabal narrated to me that you said: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah sincerely enters Paradise. He said: Mu'adh spoke the truth, Mu'adh spoke the truth, Mu'adh spoke the truth."
"18259","81 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: I was the riding companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with nothing between me and him but the rear of the saddle. He said to me: O Mu'adh. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and blessed. He said: Do you know what is the right of Allah over the servants? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The right of Allah over the servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he travelled a while, then said: O Mu'adh ibn Jabal. I said: At your service and blessed. He said: Do you know what is the right of the servants upon Allah when they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The right of the servants upon Allah is that He not punish them."
"18260","82 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Fada al-Jawhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Mu'adh. I said: At your service. He said: Give the people glad tidings that whoever says La ilaha illa Allah enters Paradise."
"18261","83 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: I was the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Mu'adh ibn Jabal, do you know what is the right of Allah over the servants? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That they associate nothing with Him. Then he said: Do you know what is their right upon Him when they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That He not punish them."
"18262","84 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Sulayman al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: We came to Mu'adh and said: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted me behind him and said: Do you know what is the right of Allah over the servants? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: His right over them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he said: Do you know, when they do that, what is their right upon Him? Their right upon Him is that He not punish them."
"18263","85 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ali ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like."
"18264","86 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas, from Mu'adh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like."
"18265","87 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We came to Mu'adh ibn Jabal and said: Narrate to us of the rare hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I was the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a donkey, and he said: O Mu'adh. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you know what is the right of Allah over the servants? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: A right upon them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he said: Do you know what is the right of the servants upon Allah when they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Their right upon Allah when they do that is that He not punish them."
"18266","88 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: We came to Mu'adh ibn Jabal and said: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes; while I rode behind him upon his donkey he said: O Mu'adh. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you know what is the right of Allah over the servants? — he mentioned the hadith."
"18267","Buraydah ibn al-Husayb al-Aslami, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal. 89 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Mu'min ibn Khalid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father who said: It reached me that Mu'adh ibn Jabal seized the devil in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I came to him and said: It reached me that you seized the devil in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to me the dates of charity, and I placed them in a room of mine; each day I found some loss in them. So I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: It is the work of the devil, so lie in wait for him. So I lay in wait for him at night; when part of the night had passed he came in the form of an elephant. When he reached the door he entered through the door's crevice in other than his form, drew near the dates and began stuffing them (in his mouth). So I tightened my clothes and seized him in the middle, saying: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. O enemy of Allah, you leapt upon the dates of charity and took them, while they (their owners) had more right to them than you. I shall surely raise you to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so he may disgrace you. So he pledged to me not to return, and I released him. In the morning I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: What did your captive do? I said: He pledged to me not to return. He said: He will return, so lie in wait for him. So I lay in wait for him the second night; he did the like, and I did the like, and he pledged to me not to return, so I released him. Then in the morning I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to inform him, and his caller called: Where is Mu'adh? He said to me: O Mu'adh, what did your captive do? I informed him, and he said: He will return, so lie in wait for him. So I lay in wait for him the third night; he did the like, and I did the like with him, and I said: O enemy of Allah, you pledged to me twice, and this is the third; I shall surely raise you to the Messenger of Allah so he may disgrace you. He said: I am a devil with a family, and I came to you only from Nasibayn; had I found anything nearer I would not have come to you. We were in this city of yours until your Companion was sent; and when two verses were revealed to him, they drove us from it, and we settled at Nasibayn: they are not recited in a house but the devil does not enter it thrice. If you release me I will teach them to you. I said: Yes. He said: Ayat al-Kursi, and the end of Surat al-Baqarah from His saying: (The Messenger has believed in what was revealed) to its end. So I released him. Then in the morning I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to inform him, and his caller called: Where is Mu'adh ibn Jabal? When I entered upon him he said to me: What did your captive do? I said: He pledged to me not to return, and I informed him of what he said. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: The wicked one spoke the truth though he is a liar. He said: So I used to recite them over it thereafter and found no loss in it."
"18268","Abu Layla al-Ansari, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal. 90 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Awf, of the people of Kufah from Banu Murrah ibn Hammam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from his father, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I commanded anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded a wife to prostrate to her husband, because of his right over her; and no woman finds the sweetness of faith until she fulfils the right of her husband, even if he asks her for herself upon a saddle-pack."
"18269","Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, from Mu'adh. 91 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, from Mu'adh and Abu Ubaydah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This affair began as mercy and prophethood, then will be mercy and caliphate; then it will be biting kingship; then it will be tyranny and despotism, and corruption in the land: they will deem lawful silk, private parts (fornication), and wine; and they will be provided upon that until they meet Allah."
"18270","92 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, the brother of Hajjaj, narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal and Abu Ubaydah who said: We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This affair began as mercy and prophethood, then caliphate and mercy; then it will be biting kingship, and despotism, and corruption in the land: they will deem lawful private parts (fornication), silk, and wines; and they will be aided upon that and provided until they meet Allah, Blessed and Exalted."
"18271","93 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hawbar ibn Muadh narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Fazari, from Makhul, from Ibn Abi Talhah al-Yamari, from Abu Thalabah al-Khushani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him when he sent him to Yemen: Whichever man apostatizes from Islam, call him to return; if he repents then accept it from him, and if he does not repent then strike his neck; and whichever woman apostatizes from Islam, call her; if she repents then accept it from her, and if she refuses then keep asking her to repent."
"18272","Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 94 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Utbah ibn Humayd al-Dabbi, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has charitably granted you one-third of your wealth at the time of your death as an addition in your lifetime, to make it a purification for your deeds."
"18273","95 - Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated; both said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that he used to perform the ablution for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cup mounted with copper, and give him drink in it."
"18274","96 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, and Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated; both said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The head of this matter is Islam, and whoever submits is safe; its pillar is prayer, and the peak of its hump is jihad, which none attains except the best of them."
"18275","Al-Lajlaj - and he has companionship - from Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him. 97 - Hafs ibn Amr ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abi al-Ward, from al-Lajlaj, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man who was saying: O Allah, I ask You for patience; he said: You have asked Allah for affliction, so ask Him for well-being. And he passed by a man who was saying: O Possessor of Majesty and Honor; he said: It has been answered for you. And he passed by a man who was saying: O Allah, I ask You for the perfection of Your blessing; he said: Do you know what the perfection of blessing is? He said: A supplication I made hoping for good; he said: Part of the perfection of blessing is seeking refuge from the Fire and entering Paradise."
"18276","98 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Hibban ibn Musa narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from al-Jurayri, from Abi al-Ward, from al-Lajlaj, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he passed by a man who was saying: O Allah, I ask You for patience; he said: You have asked Allah for affliction, so ask Allah for well-being. And he passed by a man who was saying: O Possessor of Majesty and Honor; he said: It has been answered for you, so ask. And he passed by a man who was saying: O Allah, I ask You for the perfection of blessing; he said: Son of Adam, do you know what the perfection of blessing is? He said: A supplication I made hoping thereby for good; he said: The perfection of blessing is entering Paradise and being saved from the Fire."
"18277","99 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, and Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi the judge narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated; all of them from Said al-Jurayri, from Abi al-Ward ibn Thumamah, from al-Lajlaj, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like thereof."
"18278","100 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed, from Ibn Said al-Jurayri, from Abi al-Ward ibn Thumamah, from al-Lajlaj, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like thereof."
"18279","Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah, from Muadh. 101 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha, in the expedition of Tabuk."
"18280","102 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Malik, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, that Muadh informed him that they went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Tabuk, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine Zuhr with Asr and Maghrib with Isha all together. He said: One day he delayed the prayer, then came out and prayed Zuhr and Asr together, then entered, then came out and prayed Maghrib and Isha together, then said: If Allah wills, tomorrow you will come to the spring of Tabuk, and you will reach it in the forenoon; whoever gets there should not touch any of its water until I come. He said: We came and two men had preceded us to it, and the spring was like a shoelace trickling a little water. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked them: Did you touch any of its water? They said: Yes. He rebuked them and said to them whatever Allah willed him to say. Then they scooped a little from the spring with their hands until it gathered in something, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed his face and hands in it, then returned it into it, and the spring flowed with abundant water and the people drank. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Muadh, if your life is prolonged you are about to see what is here filled with gardens. Thus al-Dabari said it, erring in it; rather it is filled with gardens."
"18281","103 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to me, from Abi al-Zubayr, the freedman of Hakim, from Amir ibn Wathilah Abu al-Tufayl, who said: I heard Muadh ibn Jabal saying: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, and he would not depart at midday until it cooled, then combine Zuhr with Asr, then halt when evening came and combine Maghrib with Isha."
"18282","104 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Muadh ibn Jabal who narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined in the expedition of Tabuk Zuhr with Asr and Maghrib with Isha until we returned."
"18283","105 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, and he used to pray Zuhr with Asr together, and Maghrib with Isha together."
"18284","106 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated, Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us; they said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated, Ashath ibn Sawwar narrated, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided Tabuk in severe heat, and combined Zuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha."
"18285","107 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; they said: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abi Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha, in the expedition of Tabuk."
"18286","108 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha, in the expedition of Tabuk."
"18287","109 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Muadh, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and he seated me behind him; I never touched anything softer than the skin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor did I find a fragrance more pleasant than the fragrance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Muadh, have you heard any sound since last night? I said: No. He said: A comer from my Lord came to me and gave me glad tidings that whoever dies from my nation associating nothing with Allah will enter Paradise. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not go out to the people and give them glad tidings? He said: Leave them, let them hasten to the path."
"18288","Al-Sunabihi, from Muadh. 110 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, who said: I heard Uqbah ibn Muslim al-Tujibi saying: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to me, from al-Sunabihi, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand one day then said: O Muadh, by Allah, I love you. Muadh said to him: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, and I, by Allah, love you. He said: I advise you, O Muadh, never to leave saying at the end of every prayer: O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well. And Muadh advised al-Sunabihi with that, and al-Sunabihi advised Abu Abd al-Rahman, and Abu Abd al-Rahman advised Uqbah ibn Muslim."
"18289","111 - Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Jandi narrated to us, Samit ibn Muadh narrated, Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Adi ibn Adi, from al-Sunabihi, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four traits: about his life, how he spent it; about his youth, how he wore it out; about his wealth, from where he earned it and how he spent it; and about his knowledge, what he did with it."
"18290","Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Muadh. 112 - Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Hadhlam al-Dimashqi, Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar, and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us; they said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Three things, whoever does them has committed a crime: whoever binds a banner without right, or disobeys his parents, or walks with an oppressor, has committed a crime. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Indeed, We will take revenge upon the criminals."
"18291","113 - Abu al-Zinba and Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us; they said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Khunays ibn Amir narrated, from Abi Qabil, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, that some people entered upon Muadh ibn Jabal while he was sick and said: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which you have not forgotten and which has not become confused to you. He said: Seat me. One of the people took his hand and some sat behind him. He said: I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which I have not forgotten and which has not become confused to me. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no prophet but that he warned his people about the Dajjal, and I warn you about the matter of the Dajjal: he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed; between his eyes is written: disbeliever, which the literate and the illiterate will read; with him are a paradise and a fire, so his fire is a paradise and his paradise is a fire."
"18292","Malik ibn Ukhaymir al-Saksaki, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 114 - Abu Husayn Muhammad ibn Husayn the judge narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated, Yahya ibn Ali narrated, from Khalid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi, from his father, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Ukhaymir al-Saksaki, from Muadh ibn Jabal who narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman to give permission in her husbands house except with his permission, nor to go out while he dislikes it, nor to abandon his bed even if he is more unjust than her, nor to desert him even if he is unjust until she comes to him and apologizes to him; if he accepts her excuse, otherwise Allah accepts her excuse."
"18293","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm al-Ashari, from Muadh; Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh. 115 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Jabir al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated; both said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled early with the people in the expedition of Tabuk; when morning came he prayed the dawn prayer with the people. I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise, and I shall not ask you about anything else. He said: Excellent, excellent; you have asked about a great matter, and it is easy for one for whom Allah intends good. Then he said: You believe in Allah and the Last Day, establish prayer, and worship Allah alone with no partner until you die upon that. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, O Muadh, I shall tell you of the head of this matter, its support, and the peak of its hump: jihad in the path of Allah. I was only commanded to fight people until they testify that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and establish prayer and give zakat; if they do that they have protected their wealth and blood from me except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, no face has paled, nor foot become dusty, in a deed seeking thereby the degrees of Paradise, after an obligatory prayer, like jihad in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"18294","116 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm narrated, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stuck out his tongue, then placed his finger upon it, and Muadh exclaimed. He said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we be taken to account for all that we say and it be written against us? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the shoulder of Muadh several times and said: May your mother bereave you, O son of the mother of Muadh; does anything throw people upon their nostrils into the fire of Hell except the harvests of their tongues?"
"18295","117 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing weighs heavier in the scale of a servant than a mount he spends upon for the path of Allah, or which is ridden in the path of Allah."
"18296","118 - Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Adawi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Imran al-Qattan informed, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise will enter Paradise hairless, beardless, kohled, aged thirty-three."
"18297","119 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, al-Muharibi narrated, from Asim ibn Mansur al-Asadi and Abdullah ibn Ziyad al-Madani, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says, when he turns from the dawn prayer before speaking: There is no god but Allah alone with no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, in His Hand is good and He is over all things Capable, ten times, he is given seven things thereby: there are written for him thereby ten good deeds, and ten evil deeds are erased from him thereby, and ten degrees are raised for him thereby, and they are equal to freeing ten slaves, and they are a protection for him from Satan, and a safeguard from the disliked, and no sin overtakes him in that day of his except associating partners with Allah; and whoever says them when he turns from the Maghrib prayer is given the like thereof in his night."
"18298","120 - Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr informed, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Makhul, from Shahr ibn Hawshab - Yazid said: I do not know but that he said: from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm - from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who loves beauty, and I love to be praised - as if fearing for himself. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What prevents you from loving to live praised and die missed? I was only sent to perfect the virtues of character."
"18299","121 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Amr ibn Waqid narrated, Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever seeks knowledge to boast thereby against the scholars, and to dispute thereby with the foolish in gatherings, will not smell the fragrance of Paradise."
"18300","Umayr ibn Hani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm. 122 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated, from his father, from Makhul, from Muadh ibn Jabal, and from Umayr ibn Hani, who heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm narrating that he heard Muadh ibn Jabal narrating, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said to him: Tell me of a deed that admits to Paradise when he does it? He said: Excellent, excellent; you have asked about a great matter, and it is easy for one for whom Allah makes it easy: you establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakat, and associate nothing with Allah."
"18301","Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh. 123 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated, from Abd al-Ala ibn Abi Amrah, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Milky Way in the sky is the sweat of the serpent beneath the Throne."
"18302","124 - Al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; they said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated, from Abi al-Atuf, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to dispatch Muadh to Yemen, he consulted some of his Companions - among them Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, and Usayd ibn Hudayr - and he consulted them. Abu Bakr said: Had you not consulted us we would not have spoken. He said: In what has not been revealed to me I am like one of you. The people spoke, each speaking his opinion. He said: What do you think, O Muadh? He said: I think what Abu Bakr said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, above His heaven, dislikes that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, should err."
"18303","125 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman narrated, from Muhammad ibn Said, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution once, twice, and three times three times; he used to do all of that."
"18304","126 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from Muhammad ibn Said, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform tayammum with earth, and I did not see him wipe his hands and face except once."
"18305","127 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, al-Ahwas ibn Hakim narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Said, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping his face with the edge of his garment in ablution."
"18306","128 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum, from Utbah ibn Humayd, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) read it: Can your Lord send down."
"18307","129 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated, and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated; both said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated, Abu Abd al-Aziz Yahya ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Urdunni narrated, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: We raided Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we took sheep; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed a portion of them among us, and that sufficed us, and he placed the remainder in the spoils."
"18308","130 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to urge his Companions to single combat."
"18309","131 - Musa ibn Hazim al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami narrated, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm al-Ashari, who said: When Shurahbil ibn Hasanah conquered Qinnasrin he took cattle and sheep there, and distributed them among the people, and remnants remained, so he put their price into the spoils. Ibn Ghanm said: I narrated it to Muadh and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed among us the livestock of Khaybar, and remnants of it remained, so he sold them and put their price into the shares."
"18310","132 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum, from Utbah ibn Humayd, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was skinning a sheep, and said to me: O Muadh, give - or show me - and he thrust it twice between the flesh and the skin, then said: O Muadh, like this. Then he went to prayer."
"18311","133 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Harun ibn Maruf narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated, Bakr ibn Khunays informed, from Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, who said: I asked Muadh ibn Jabal: Do you use the tooth-stick while fasting? He said: Yes. I said: At which part of the day do you use it? He said: At whichever part of the day you wish; if you wish in the morning, and if you wish in the evening. I said: People dislike it in the evening. He said: Why? I said: They say the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The breath of the fasting person is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk. He said: Glory be to Allah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them with the tooth-stick when he commanded them, knowing that the mouth of the fasting person must have some breath even if he uses the tooth-stick; he would not command them to deliberately make their mouths foul, for there is no good in that, rather evil in it, except one afflicted with an affliction from which he finds no escape. I said: And dust in the path of Allah is likewise? One is only rewarded therein who is compelled to it and finds no escape from it? He said: Yes; as for one who throws himself into affliction deliberately, he has no reward from that."
"18312","134 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Busr narrated, from Mutarrif ibn Mazin, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Abi al-Hakam al-Dimashqi, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only commanded ablution from what fire has altered by washing the hands and mouth for cleanliness, and it is not obligatory."
"18313","135 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Rawahah al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum, from Utbah ibn Humayd, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and Muadh ibn Jabal narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A pregnant woman, if she kills deliberately, is not killed until she delivers what is in her womb and it is cared for; and if she commits adultery she is not stoned until she delivers what is in her womb and it is cared for."
"18314","Ismail ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi al-Muhajir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm. 136 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Balabakki narrated to us, my father narrated, and Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Balabakki narrated, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ismail ibn Ubaydullah, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm narrated to us, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever recites the Quran and acts upon what is in it and dies in the congregation, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection with the scribes and the rulers; whoever recites the Quran while it slips from him, yet he does not abandon it, has his reward twice; whoever is keen upon it though unable, yet does not abandon it, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection with the nobles of his family, and they will be favored over creatures as eagles are favored over other birds, and as a spring in a meadow is favored over what is around it. Then a caller will call: Where are those whom tending livestock did not divert from reciting My Book? They will stand, and one of them will wear the crown of honor, and be given success in his right hand and eternity in his left; if his parents are Muslims they will be clothed with a robe better than the world and what is in it, and they will say: How is this for us? It will be said: For what your child used to recite of the Quran."
"18315","Ayyub ibn Kurayz, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm. 137 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated, and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiy narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated; both said: Mubarak ibn Said, brother of Sufyan ibn Said, narrated, Said ibn Masruq narrated, from Ayyub ibn Kurayz, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: While we were a company with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his mount went ahead, then my mount caught up with his mount until I thought his mount had recognized the tread of my mount, until my knee struck his knee. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wanted to ask you many times, but the place of this verse prevents me: O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if made plain to you, may trouble you. He said: What is it, O Muadh? I said: The deed that admits to Paradise and keeps me away from the Fire. He said: You have asked about a great matter, and it is easy: testimony that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakat, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan. Then he said: Shall I not tell you of the head of this matter, its pillar, and its peak is jihad. Then he said: Fasting is a shield, and charity expiates sins. Then he said: Shall I not inform you of what controls people over that? He took his tongue and placed it between two of his fingers. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is all that we speak written against us? He said: May your mother bereave you; does anything throw people upon their nostrils into the Fire except the harvests of their tongues? You remain safe so long as you are silent; when you speak it is written for you or against you."
"18316","Imran ibn Muslim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm. 138 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated, Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated, al-Khasib ibn Jahdar narrated, from Imran ibn Muslim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with whom he loves."
"18317","Al-Numan ibn Nuaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm. 139 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Salih ibn Abdullah al-Tirmidhi narrated, Mahbub ibn al-Hasan al-Qurashi narrated, from al-Khasib ibn Jahdar, from al-Numan ibn Nuaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he was in his prayer, would raise his hands opposite his ears; when he said the takbir he would let them down, then be silent, and sometimes I saw him placing his right upon his left. When he finished the Opening of the Book he would be silent, and when he completed the chapter he would be silent, then raise his hands opposite his ears, say the takbir and bow, and we would not bow until we saw him bowing. Then he would stand straight from his bowing until every limb took its place, then raise his hands opposite his ears, say the takbir and fall prostrate, and he would press his forehead and nose firmly upon the ground. Then he would rise like an arrow without leaning upon his hands. When he sat at the end of his prayer he would lean upon his left thigh, his right hand upon his right thigh, and point with his finger when supplicating. When he gave the salutation he would rise quickly."
"18318","Al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm. 140 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah and Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Hutiyyan narrated to us; they said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim narrated, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted a donkey of his called Yafur, its bridle of palm-fiber, and said: Ride, O Muadh. I said: Go on, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Ride. So he seated me behind him, and the donkey threw us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood laughing, then mounted a second time and said: Ride. So I rode, and the donkey carried us as Allah willed. He reached back with his hand and struck my back with a whip he had - or a stick - and said: O Muadh, son of the mother of Muadh, do you know what is the right of Allah upon people? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The right of Allah upon servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he traveled as Allah willed, then reached back with his hand and struck my back, and said: O Muadh, son of the mother of Muadh, do you know what is the right of servants upon Allah when they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The right of servants upon Allah is that He admit them to Paradise when they do that."
"18319","141 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah and Abu Zayd al-Hutiyyan narrated to us; they said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim narrated, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm al-Ashari, Muadh ibn Jabal narrated to me, who said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he raided Tabuk, he traveled late one night and we traveled late with him, then he prayed dawn and we prayed with him, then he went in the morning and we went with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled and the companies and camels scattered grazing with their mouths, and upon him was a Najrani cloak. My eye caught the ring of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was dozing, and I thought revelation would descend upon him. While I was thus, my she-camel let out a bray and spoiled it, its foreleg twisted, and the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was startled by its striking, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke, turned and saw me, and said: O Muadh. I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Come near. So I came near; he said that three times, and I came near until the two mounts came together. Muadh said: In myself was a word that had seized me and distressed me which I had not asked you about, and I had not heard anyone asking you about it. He said: Ask me, O Muadh. I said: Tell me, O Messenger of Allah, of a deed that admits me to Paradise. He said: Excellent, excellent; you have asked about a great matter, though it is easy: you testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish prayer, pay zakat, and worship Allah alone. Then I turned to him asking. I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? Prayer after prayer? He said: No, and yes, what a thing it is. I said: O Messenger of Allah, zakat after the obligatory zakat? He said: No, and yes, what a thing it is. I said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting after the obligatory fasting? He said: No, and yes, what a thing it is. He said: Shall I not tell you, O Muadh, of the head of this matter, its support, and the peak of its hump? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The head of this matter is testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, its support is establishing prayer and giving zakat, and the peak of its hump is jihad in the path of Allah. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, never have the feet or face of a servant become dusty in a deed better with Allah after that. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"18320","142 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Harun ibn al-Mughirah al-Razi narrated, my father narrated, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated, from Sad ibn Khalid, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab employed Muadh ibn Jabal over Syria, and wrote to him: Give people their stipends, and raid with them. While he was giving people - and that was at the end of time - a man from the people of the countryside came and said: O Muadh, order my stipend for me, for I am a man from the people of the countryside from such-and-such place; perhaps I may reach my family before night. He said: No, by Allah, I shall not give you until I give these - meaning the people of the city. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: All the prophets will enter Paradise forty years before Sulayman ibn Dawud, the poor Muslims will enter Paradise forty years before their rich, the righteous slaves will enter Paradise forty years before others, and the people of cities will enter Paradise forty years before the people of the countryside by virtue of cities, congregations, Fridays, circles of remembrance; and when there is affliction they are singled out with it apart from them."
"18321","An unnamed man, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm. 143 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from a man who narrated to him, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glad tidings to one who increases in jihad in the path of Allah the remembrance of Allah, for he has for every word seventy thousand good deeds, each good deed tenfold, besides what he has with Allah of increase. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about spending? He said: Spending is in proportion to that. Abd al-Rahman said: I said to Muadh: Spending is only seven hundredfold. Muadh said: Your understanding is little; that is only when they spend while residing among their families, not raiding; when they raid and spend, Allah stores for them from the treasury of His mercy what the knowledge and description of servants cannot reach. Those are the party of Allah, and the party of Allah are the victorious."
"18322","Abu Idris al-Khawlani Aidhullah ibn Abdullah, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 144 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us; they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: Aidhullah narrated to me, who said: I said to Muadh: I love you, and I love your hadith. He said: Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Those who love one another for the majesty of Allah will be in the shade of the Throne of Allah on the Day of Resurrection, when there is no shade except His shade."
"18323","145 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those who love one another for Allah will be in His shade on a day when there is no shade except His shade."
"18324","146 - Khayr ibn Arafah al-Misri narrated to us, Urwah ibn Marwan al-Raqqi narrated, Shuayb ibn Zurayq narrated, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Those who love one another for the majesty of Allah will be in the shade of the Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade."
"18325","147 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Baqiyyah narrated, Utbah ibn Abi Hakim narrated, Ata al-Khurasani narrated to me, Abu Idris al-Khawlani narrated to me, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Those who love one another for Allah will be in the shade of the Throne."
"18326","148 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Those who love one another for the majesty of Allah will be in the shade of Allah on a day when there is no shade except His shade."
"18327","149 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, who said: I heard Aidhullah Abu Idris al-Khawlani saying: I said to Muadh ibn Jabal: I love you for Allah. He took my waist and drew me to him, then said: By Allah, do you love me? I said: By Allah, I love you for Allah. He said: Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Those who love one another will be in the shade of His Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade."
"18328","150 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated, from Malik, from Abi Hazim ibn Dinar, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, that he said: I entered the mosque of Damascus, and there was a youth with bright teeth, long in silence; when people differed about something they referred it to him and issued from his opinion. I asked about him and it was said: Muadh ibn Jabal. Next day I came early and found he had preceded me in coming early, and found him praying. I waited until he finished his prayer, then came to him from before his face, greeted him, and said: By Allah, I love you for Allah. He said: By Allah? I said: By Allah. He said: By Allah? I said: By Allah. He said: By Allah? I said: By Allah. He said: He took the fold of my cloak and drew me to him, and said: Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah said: My love is due for those who love one another for Me, sit together for Me, spend for one another for Me, and visit one another for Me."
"18329","151 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, my father narrated, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Aidhullah ibn Abdullah, who said: I heard Muadh ibn Jabal saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Those who love one another for Allah will be in the shade of the Throne of Allah on a day when there is no shade except His shade."
"18330","152 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad al-Maqdisi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Abu Mashar narrated, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, who said: I entered the mosque of Hims and there were men narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); among them a youth with dark eyes and bright teeth; when he spoke the people all listened to his speech, and when they disputed they accepted his word therein; and he was Muadh ibn Jabal. We sat with him and I said: I love you. He took my cloak-fold and drew me to him until my knee touched his knee, then said: Shall I not give you glad tidings from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), reporting from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, who said: My love is due for those who love one another, sit together, visit one another, and spend for one another for Me."
"18331","153 - Abdullah ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated, Abu Mashar narrated, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), reporting from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, who said: My love is due for those who love one another and sit together, and spend for one another for Me."
"18332","154 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Those who love one another for Allah will be in the shade of the Throne of Allah on a day when there is no shade except His shade; people will panic and they will not panic, people will fear and they will not fear. He said: I stood from him and came to Ubadah ibn al-Samit, and Ubadah said: And better than it: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: My love is rightfully due for those who love one another for Me, and My love is rightfully due for those who sit together for Me, and My love is rightfully due for those who visit one another for Me."
"18333","155 - Muhammad ibn Abi Zurah and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Dimashqiyyan narrated to us; they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Amr ibn Waqid narrated, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah brighten a servant who hears my speech then does not add to it; many a carrier of understanding to one more comprehending than him. Three things over which the heart of a believer does not harbor deceit: sincerity of deed for Allah, sincere advice to those in authority, and adherence to the congregation of Muslims, for their supplication encompasses those behind them."
"18334","156 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated, Amr ibn Waqid narrated, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a deed which, when I do it, I shall enter Paradise? He said: Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are burned; obey your parents, even if they remove you from your wealth; do not drink wine, for it is the key to every evil; never abandon prayer deliberately, for whoever abandons prayer deliberately, the protection of Allah is free of him; do not dispute authority with its people even if you see that it is yours; spend upon your family from your means; do not lift the stick from them; make them fear Allah; do not misappropriate; do not flee from the battle line."
"18335","157 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, and Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated; both said: Amr ibn Waqid narrated, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abi Idris, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The first thing my Lord forbade me after worship of idols is drinking wine, and quarreling with men."
"18336","158 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated, and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated; both said: Amr ibn Waqid narrated, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abi Idris, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: On the Day of Resurrection there will be brought the one whose intellect was removed, the one who perished in the interval, and the one who perished young. The one whose intellect was removed will say: My Lord, had You given me intellect, none given intellect would have been happier with his intellect than me. The one who perished young will say: My Lord, had You given me life, none given life would have been happier with his life than me. The one who perished in the interval will say: My Lord, had a messenger from You come to me, no human to whom a covenant from You came would have been happier with Your covenant than me. The Lord, Exalted, will say: I command you with a command; will you obey Me? They will say: Yes, by Your might, O Lord. He will say: Go and enter Hell - and had they entered it, it would not harm them at all. Then flames from the Fire will come out upon them, which they will think has destroyed everything Allah created. Then He will command them a second time and they will return likewise. The Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will say: I created you with My knowledge, and to My knowledge you shall return; then the Fire will seize them."
"18337","159 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated; both said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, Zayd ibn Waqid narrated, from Busr ibn Ubaydullah, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you about the kings of the people of Paradise? They said: Yes. He said: Every weak, oppressed one with two worn garments, not regarded; if he swears by Allah, Allah fulfills it."
"18338","160 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated, and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated; both said: Amr ibn Waqid narrated, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day mentioned tribulations, magnifying and stressing them. Ali ibn Abi Talib said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the way out of them? He said: The Book of Allah; in it is the account of those before you, the tidings of those after you, and the criterion between you. Whoever abandons it among the tyrants, Allah breaks him; whoever seeks guidance in other than it, Allah misguides him. It is the firm rope of Allah, the Wise Remembrance, and the Straight Path. When the jinn heard it they said: Indeed, we have heard a wondrous Quran. It is that by which tongues do not differ, and much repetition does not wear it out."
"18339","161 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated, and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated; both said: Amr ibn Waqid narrated, from Yunus ibn Maysarah, from Abi Idris, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, whoever believes in me, affirms me, and testifies that what I came with is the truth, lessen his wealth and children and hasten his taking to You; and whoever does not believe in me, affirm me, and know that what I came with is the truth from You, increase his wealth and children and prolong his life."
"18340","162 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated, and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated; both said: Amr ibn Waqid narrated, from Yunus ibn Maysarah, from Abi Idris, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever feeds a believer until he satisfies him from hunger, Allah admits him through a gate of Paradise which none enters except one like him."
"18341","163 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Amr ibn Waqid narrated, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abi Idris, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient one; whoever meets Allah breaking his pledge meets Him leprous; whoever leaves the congregation deliberately a handspan has removed the yoke of Islam from his neck; whoever dies with no obedience to a leader of the congregation upon him dies a death of ignorance."
"18342","164 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Amr ibn Waqid narrated, Yunus ibn Maysarah narrated, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The banner of the treacherous one on the Day of Resurrection will be at his backside."
"18343","165 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated, and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated; both said: Amr ibn Waqid narrated, Yunus ibn Maysarah narrated, from Abi Idris, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown that I was placed in a scale, and my nation in a scale, and I outweighed it; then Abu Bakr was placed in a scale and my nation in a scale, and he outweighed it; and Umar was placed in a scale and my nation in a scale, and he outweighed it; and Uthman was placed in a scale and he outweighed it; then the scale was lifted."
"18344","166 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, Aidhullah ibn Abdullah narrated to me that Muadh ibn Jabal came to them in Yemen, and a woman from Khawlan met him with twelve sons of hers, leaving their father in their house, the youngest of whom had a full beard. She stood, greeted Muadh - two of her sons holding her upper arm - and said: Who sent you, O man? Muadh said to her: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me. The woman said: The Messenger of Allah sent you, and you are the messenger of the Messenger of Allah? Will you not tell me, O messenger of the Messenger of Allah, what is the right of a husband over his wife? Muadh said: She fears Allah as much as she can, and hears and obeys. She said: I adjure you to tell me what is the right of a husband over his wife? Muadh said to her: Are you not content to hear and obey, and fear Allah? She said: Yes, but I left the father of these as an old man in the house. Muadh said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muadh, if you were to return to him and find leprosy had eaten his flesh and pierced his nostrils, and find his nostrils flowing with pus and blood, then cast them into your mouth to fulfill his right, you would never fulfill that ever."
"18345","Abu Muslim al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 167 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me; both said: Waki narrated, Jafar ibn Burqan narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Marzuq, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abi Muslim al-Khawlani, who said: I came to the mosque of Damascus and there was a circle with elders from the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and among them a youth with kohled eyes and bright teeth; whenever they differed about something they referred it to the youth. I said to my companion: Who is this? He said: Muadh ibn Jabal. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Those who love one another for Allah will be upon pulpits of light in the shade of the Throne of the Most Merciful on a day when there is no shade except His shade."
"18346","168 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated, Abu al-Malih narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Marzuq, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abi Muslim al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Those who love one another will be in the shade of the Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade, upon pulpits of light; the prophets and the truthful will envy them for their place."
"18347","Madikarib, from Muadh. 169 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated, and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Jafar al-Ramli narrated; both said: Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Matar al-Warraq, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Madikarib, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most fearful of what I fear for my nation are three: a man who read the Book of Allah until, when you see brightness upon him and the cloak of Islam upon him - which Allah lent him - he draws his sword and strikes his neighbor with it and accuses him of polytheism. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, is the accuser more deserving of it or the accused? He said: The accuser. And a man to whom Allah gives authority and he says: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah - and he lies; no caliph may be a shield apart from the Creator. And a man whom narrations carry away; whenever he finishes one story he narrates a longer one; if he lives to the Dajjal he will follow him."
"18348","Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 170 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated, Yahya ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Urdunni narrated, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: We raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we took sheep; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed a portion of them among us, and placed the remainder in the spoils."
"18349","Yazid ibn Qutayb, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 171 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Huti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated, Safwan ibn Amr narrated, Abu Ziyad Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Ghassani narrated, from Yazid ibn Qutayb, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen and said: Perhaps you will pass by my mosque and my grave; I have sent you to a people tender-hearted, who fight upon the truth; so fight with those of them who obey you those who disobey you, then they will return to Islam until the wife hastens to her husband, the child to his father, and the brother to his brother; so alight between the two tribes of al-Sakun and al-Sakasik."
"18350","Yazid ibn Marthad, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 172 - Al-Qasim ibn Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Balkhi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hujr al-Marwazi narrated, and Khattab ibn Said al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated; both said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Yazid ibn Marthad, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Take the gift so long as it is a gift; when it becomes a bribe in religion, do not take it; yet you will not leave it, poverty and need preventing you. Verily the millstone of Islam is turning, so turn with the Book wherever it turns. Verily the Book and authority will part, so do not part from the Book. Verily there will be rulers over you who decree for themselves what they do not decree for you; if you disobey them they will kill you, and if you obey them they will misguide you. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall we do? He said: As the companions of Isa son of Maryam did: they were sawn with saws and carried upon wood; death in obedience to Allah is better than life in disobedience to Allah."
"18351","Abu Bahriyyah, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 173 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abi Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Abi Bahriyyah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The great battle, the conquest of Constantinople, and the emergence of the Dajjal will be in seven months."
"18352","174 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abi Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from al-Walid ibn Sufyan, from Yazid ibn Qutayb, from Abi Bahriyyah, from Muadh, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The great battle, the conquest of Constantinople, and the emergence of the Dajjal will be in seven months."
"18353","175 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated, from al-Walid ibn Sufyan, from Yazid ibn Qutayb, from Abi Bahriyyah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like thereof."
"18354","176 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Huti narrated to us, my father narrated, and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated; both said: Baqiyyah informed, and Khayr ibn Arafah narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, Baqiyyah narrated, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abi Bahriyyah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Campaigning is of two kinds: as for one who campaigns seeking the Face of Allah, obeys the leader, spends the precious, consoles his partner, and avoids corruption in the land, his sleep and wakefulness are all good; as for one who campaigns for pride, show and repute, disobeys the leader, and corrupts in the land, he does not return even with bare sufficiency."
"18355","177 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Huti narrated to us, my father narrated, Baqiyyah narrated, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abi Bahriyyah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Night of Decree, and said: It is in the last ten, on the seventh, or the fifth, or the third."
"18356","178 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Ubaydullah narrated, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abi Bahriyyah, who said: I came to Syria to Muadh ibn Jabal and said: I love you for Allah. He took my garment and drew me, and said: By Allah? - twice or thrice - I said: By Allah. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: My love - or My mercy - is due for those who love one another for Me, sit together for Me, visit one another and spend for one another for Me."
"18357","Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 179 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abdullah ibn Amir al-Aslami narrated, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge with Allah from greed leading to avarice, from greed toward what offers no satisfaction, and from greed toward where there is no greed."
"18358","180 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Ammar ibn Kab Abu Kab narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from Abi al-Zahiriyyah, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting."
"18359","181 - Ahmad ibn Abi Yahya al-Hadrami al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Afiyah ibn Ayyub narrated, my grandfather Afiyah ibn Ayyub narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are most beloved to Allah, Exalted? He said: That you die with your tongue moist from the remembrance of Allah."
"18360","182 - Abu Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Misri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Yazid ibn Yahya Abu Khalid narrated, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise do not regret except for an hour that passed them in which they did not remember Allah."
"18361","Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 183 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Said ibn Sallam al-Attar narrated, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek help in attaining needs through secrecy, for every possessor of blessing is envied."
"18362","184 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Qatadah ibn al-Fadl ibn Qatadah al-Rahawi narrated, who said: I heard Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do you know what Allah says to the believers on the Day of Resurrection, and the first thing they say? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: He says to the believers on the Day of Resurrection: Did you love meeting Me? They say: Yes, O Lord; we hoped for Your pardon and forgiveness. He said: I have made My pardon and forgiveness due for you."
"18363","185 - Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Adam al-Asqalani and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; they said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi narrated, Utbah ibn al-Sakan al-Fazari narrated, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats, drinks, or shoots game and forgets to mention Allah, let him eat thereof so long as he did not abandon the mention deliberately."
"18364","186 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hoarding, what it is? He said: When he hears of cheapness it grieves him, and when he hears of high prices he rejoices at it. Evil is the hoarding servant: if Allah cheapens prices he grieves, and if He raises them he rejoices."
"18365","187 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi narrated, Utbah ibn al-Sakan al-Fazari narrated, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If my nation knew what it has in fenugreek, they would seek it even for its weight in gold."
"18366","188 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated, and Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi narrated; both said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever walks to a man of innovation to honor him has aided in demolishing Islam."
"18367","189 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, Abu Abdullah - a man from al-Anbar - narrated, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about borrowing yeast and bread, and said: Glory be to Allah; it is among the noble traits of character: take the small and give the large, take the large and give the small, and the best of you is the best in repayment."
"18368","190 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Hilali narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Sallam al-Tawil narrated, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O people, take the fear of Allah as merchandise; provision will come to you without goods or trade. Then he recited: And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out, and provide for him from where he does not expect."
"18369","191 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ismah ibn Sulayman al-Khazzaz narrated, Hazim, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated, from Limazah, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attended the wedding feast of a man from his Companions, and said to him: Upon good, affection, auspicious fortune, and abundance in provision; may Allah bless you; beat the tambourine over his head. A tambourine was brought and beaten, and dishes came with fruit and sugar upon them, and it was scattered over him. People withheld their hands. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why do you not plunder? They said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not forbid plundering? He said: I only forbade you the plundering of armies; as for weddings, no. He said: He tussled with them and they tussled with him."
"18370","192 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Salamah ibn Shabib narrated, Abd al-Razzaq narrated, Thawr ibn Yazid informed me, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in our house displaying horses. Uyaynah ibn Hisn entered upon him and said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You are more discerning of horses than I, and I am more discerning of men than you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which men are best? He said: Men who carry their swords upon their shoulders, display their spears upon the withers of their horses, and wear striped cloaks, from the people of Najd. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You lie; the best of men are the men of Yemen; faith is Yemeni, and the largest tribe in Paradise is Madhhij; the eaten of Himyar is from its eater; Hadramawt is better than Kindah. May Allah curse the four kings: Jamad, Mishrah, Mihwas, Abd, and their sister al-Amarradah."
"18371","193 - Wathilah ibn al-Hasan al-Awfi narrated to us, Kathir ibn Ubayd al-Hadhdha narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to perform ablution so long as water has not become stagnant, turning green or yellow."
"18372","Abd al-Rahman ibn Aidh al-Azdi, from Muadh. 194 - Abu Abd al-Malik Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Huti narrated to us, my father narrated, and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated; they said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Khuzai narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aidh, that a man asked Muadh ibn Jabal about what makes bathing obligatory from intercourse, about prayer in a single garment, and about what is lawful for a menstruating woman from her husband? Muadh said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that and he said: When the circumcised passes the circumcised, bathing is obligatory; as for prayer in a single garment, wrap yourself with it; as for what is lawful from the menstruating woman, what is above the waist-wrapper is lawful from her, and abstaining from that is better."
"18373","195 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman narrated, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated, Abu al-Ayyash narrated that he asked Muadh ibn Jabal what makes bathing obligatory, and whether he eats with his wife while she is menstruating? He said: You asked me about what I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about, and he said: Bathing is obligatory from major impurity."
"18374","Abu Abdullah al-Ashari, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 196 - Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; they said: Amr ibn Hisham Abu Umayyah al-Harrani narrated, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taraiqi narrated, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Abi Abdullah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever binds the jizyah upon his neck has dissociated from what Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with."
"18375","Al-Hasan ibn Jabir al-Qurashi, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 197 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, Uqayl ibn Mudrik narrated, from Luqman ibn Amir, from al-Hasan ibn Jabir al-Qurashi, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that he heard a rustling, seized it and said: Who are you? He said: I am a devil. He said: Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Leave me, for I shall not return. So he let him go. Next morning he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: O Muadh, what did your captive do? He said: I released him. On the second night he sensed him and seized him; he pleaded again and swore not to return, so he let him go. On the third night he sensed him, seized him, and he pleaded again and swore not to return; he refused to release him. He said: Let me go until I teach you a verse which, when you recite it, we shall not approach that place; and he taught him Ayat al-Kursi. So he let him go, and came in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him what happened. He said: He told the truth though he is a liar."
"18376","Abu Shaybah, from Muadh. 198 - Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn al-Harish al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated, Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abi al-Fayd, who said: I heard Aba Shaybah saying: Muadh was walking with a man with him, and lifted a stone from the road. He said: What is this? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lifts a stone from the road, a good deed is written for him; and whoever has a good deed enters Paradise."
"18377","Al-Hajjaj ibn Uthman al-Saksaki, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 199 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Huti narrated to us, my father narrated, and Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Utbah narrated; both said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Safwan ibn Amr, al-Hajjaj ibn Uthman al-Saksaki narrated to us, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing praying; he remained standing until morning, then prostrated a prostration in which I thought his soul was taken. He looked at me and said: O Muadh, did you see? I said: O Messenger of Allah, yes; I saw you prostrate a prostration in which I thought your soul was taken. He said: Do you know why that was? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: I prayed what my Lord prescribed for me, and my Lord came to me and said: O Muhammad, what shall I do with your nation? I said: My Lord, You know best. He repeated it to me three or four times, and said to me at the last of it: What shall I do with your nation? I said: You know best, O Lord. He said: I shall not grieve you concerning your nation. So I prostrated to my Lord; and your Lord is Grateful, loving the grateful."
"18378","Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 200 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi the judge narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed whose doer enters Paradise. He said: Excellent, excellent; you have asked about a great matter, and it is easy for one for whom Allah makes it easy: you worship Allah associating nothing with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakat, fast Ramadan, and perform pilgrimage to the House. And I shall tell you of the head of this matter, its pillar, and the peak of its hump: the head of this matter is testimony that there is no god but Allah, its pillar and the peak of its hump is jihad. And I shall tell you of the gates of good: fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire, and a servant standing at night. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: Their sides forsake their beds. The verse. And I shall tell you of what controls all that. He moved his mount, and I drew near people, then drew near him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is that which controls all that? He pointed with his hand to his tongue. I said: The tongue? As if making light of it. He said: May your mother bereave you, O Muadh ibn Jabal; does anything throw people into the fire of Hell except the harvests of their tongues?"
"18379","201 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No caution avails against decree, but supplication avails against what has befallen and what has not befallen; so upon you is supplication, O servants of Allah."
"18380","202 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the noble of a people comes to you, honor him."
"18381","Malik ibn Yakhamir al-Saksaki, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 203 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Huti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated, and Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated; both said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever fights in the path of Allah for the time between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise is due for him; and the time between two milkings of a she-camel is the measure of milk she yields for one who milks her."
"18382","204 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, Malik ibn Yakhamir al-Saksaki narrated to us that Muadh ibn Jabal narrated to them that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever fights in the path of Allah, a Muslim man, for the time between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise is due for him; whoever asks Allah for death sincerely from himself, then dies or is killed, has the reward of a martyr; if he is wounded in the path of Allah or suffers a mishap, it will be on the Day of Resurrection in color like saffron and scent like musk; whoever is wounded in the path of Allah bears the seal of martyrs."
"18383","205 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zurah narrated, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks Allah for death sincerely from himself, then dies or is killed, has the reward of a martyr; whoever is wounded in the path of Allah or suffers a mishap, it will come on the Day of Resurrection in color like saffron and scent like musk; whoever is wounded in the path of Allah bears the seal of martyrs."
"18384","206 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated, from his father, from Makhul, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fights in the path of Allah for the time between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise is due for him; whoever asks for death sincerely from himself, then dies or is killed, has the reward of a martyr; whoever is wounded in the path of Allah or suffers a mishap, it will come on the Day of Resurrection at its fullest as it was, in color like saffron and scent like musk."
"18385","207 - Abu Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir narrated, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated, and Ahmad ibn Anas ibn Malik al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay narrated, Zayd ibn Waqid narrated, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, that Muadh ibn Jabal narrated to them that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever fights in the path of Allah for the time between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise is due for him; whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely from his heart in the path of Allah, Paradise is due for him; whoever is wounded in the path of Allah or suffers a mishap, it will come on the Day of Resurrection at its fullest as it was, in color like saffron and scent like musk; whoever has wounds in the path of Allah is sealed with the seal of martyrs."
"18386","208 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Amir al-Nahwi al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated, from his father, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that Malik ibn Yakhamir narrated to them that Muadh ibn Jabal said to them: The last words upon which I parted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were that I said: Which deeds are most beloved to Allah? He said: That you die with your tongue moist from the remembrance of Allah."
"18387","209 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, my father narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Ibn Thawban, from his father, from Makhul, referring it to al-Harith ibn al-Harith, that Malik ibn Yakhamir narrated to them, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No soul dies having with Allah even an ant-weight of good except it is sealed over with clay."
"18388","210 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated, Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated, from Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani, from his father, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is not lawful for a woman to give permission in her husbands house while he dislikes it, nor to go out while he dislikes it, nor to obey anyone therein against him, nor to embitter his heart, nor to abandon his bed, nor to strike him, even if he is more unjust than her, until she pleases him; if he is pleased and accepts from her, then well and good: Allah accepts her excuse, brightens her face, and there is no sin upon her; if he refuses to be pleased with her, she has conveyed her excuse."
"18389","211 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qatiyi narrated, Bishr ibn Umar al-Zahrani narrated, from Shuayb ibn Zurayq, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like thereof."
"18390","212 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Muqri narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated, from his father, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are most beloved to Allah? He said: That you die with your tongue moist from the remembrance of Allah."
"18391","213 - Ahmad ibn Abi Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Afiyah narrated, my grandfather Afiyah ibn Ayyub narrated, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, al-Ala ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like thereof."
"18392","214 - Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated; both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated, from his father, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The flourishing of Bayt al-Maqdis is the ruin of Yathrib, the ruin of Yathrib is the emergence of the great battle, the emergence of the great battle is the conquest of Constantinople, and the conquest of Constantinople is the emergence of the Dajjal."
"18393","215 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid narrated, Utbah ibn Hammad narrated, from al-Awzai and Ibn Thawban, from his father, from Makhul, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, looks upon His creation on the night of the middle of Shaban and forgives all His creation except a polytheist or one harboring rancor."
"18394","216 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Awaqi narrated, Jahdam ibn Abdullah al-Yamami narrated, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Khuzai narrated, Musa ibn Khalaf al-Ammi narrated; both said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather Mamtur, from Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Saksaki, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the dawn prayer for us until the sun was about to rise; when he prayed dawn with us he said: Tonight I prayed what was decreed for me, and laid my side in the mosque; my Lord came to me in the best form and said: O Muhammad, do you know concerning what the highest assembly disputes? I said: No, O Lord. He said it three times. I said: No, O Lord. He placed His hand between my shoulders and I felt its coolness between my breasts, and everything became manifest to me and I knew it. I said: Concerning degrees and expiations. He said: What are degrees? I said: Feeding food, spreading peace, and prayer while people sleep. He said: You spoke truly. He said: What are expiations? I said: Completing ablution in cold hardships, awaiting prayer after prayer, and moving feet to Fridays. He said: You spoke truly. He said: Ask, O Muhammad. He said: I said: O Allah, I ask You for doing good deeds, abandoning evil deeds, loving the poor, that You forgive me and have mercy upon me; and when You intend a trial among Your servants, take me to You untempted. O Allah, I ask You for Your love, the love of one who loves You, and the love of a deed that brings me near to Your love. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn them and study them, for they are true."
"18395","217 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qassas narrated, Isa ibn Shuayb narrated, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I guarantee a house in the outskirts of Paradise, a house in the middle of Paradise, and a house in the highest Paradise for one who abandons disputation though right, abandons lying though jesting, and whose character is good."
"18396","218 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, my father narrated, and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and said: I love you, O Muadh. I said: And I, by Allah, love you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I advise you with words to say at the end of every prayer: My Lord, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well."
"18397","219 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Zibriq ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, my father narrated, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, returning that to a certain heart, enters Paradise."
"18398","220 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to me, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to me; both said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, Bahir ibn Sad narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, after coming to Medina, toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months; then Allah sent down a verse commanding him to turn to the Kabah, and said: We see the turning of your face toward heaven. The verse."
"18399","Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, from Muadh. 221 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has as his last speech: There is no god but Allah, enters Paradise."
"18400","222 - Al-Walid ibn Hammad al-Ramli narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Sadan ibn Yahya narrated, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for lepers, do not gaze at them continually."
"18401","223 - Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, Sadan ibn Yahya narrated, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: He is Allah, One, equals a third of the Quran."
"18402","224 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq narrated to us, my father Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to me, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to me; both said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, Bahir ibn Sad narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No woman harms her husband in this world but his wife from the wide-eyed houris says: Do not harm him, may Allah fight you; he is only a guest with you, about to part from you to us."
"18403","225 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi and Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us; both said: Hisham ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani narrated, from Ibn Thawban, from his father, from Makhul, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will halt at a station called al-Jabiyah - or al-Jubiyyah - where a disease like the gland of a camel will befall you; Allah will thereby martyr your souls and offspring, and purify thereby your deeds."
"18404","Amr ibn al-Aswad, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 226 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated, Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated, from Nasr ibn Alqamah, from his brother, from Ibn Aidh, Amr ibn al-Aswad narrated to me, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the most hateful of creation to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is one who believes then disbelieves."
"18405","Yazid ibn Umayrah, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 227 - Abu Khalifah and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us; they said: Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Humayd al-Tawil narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Yazid ibn Umayrah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: There will be tribulations in which wealth increases, and the Quran is opened so that man, woman, young, old, believer and hypocrite recite it, yet it is not followed. He will say: By Allah, I shall recite it openly, yet it is not followed. He will head to a mosque and invent speech not from the Book of Allah nor from the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Beware of him, for it is a misguiding innovation; beware of him, for it is a misguiding innovation; beware of him, for it is a misguiding innovation."
"18406","228 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Imran al-Jarmi narrated, Anas ibn Sawwar narrated, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abi Qilabah, from Yazid ibn Umayrah al-Hamdani, Muadh ibn Jabal narrated to me in his bequest in which he died, inclining to him at times, then recovering, until he was overcome with a fainting we feared he had been taken. He said: He recovered and I was facing him weeping. He said: What makes you weep? I said: By Allah, I do not weep for worldly gain from you, nor kinship between me and you, but I weep for what I used to hear from you now departing. He said: Do not weep; knowledge and faith are such: whoever seeks them finds them. Seek knowledge where Ibrahim sought it, for he asked Allah and was not forgotten. Seek it after me with four men; if you do not find it with them, then search people: seek knowledge with Abdullah ibn Masud, Abu al-Darda, Salman, and Abdullah ibn Salam. Beware the deviation of the wise, for Satan casts misguiding wisdom upon the tongue of the wise man; take knowledge when it comes to you. He said: I said to Muadh ibn Jabal: How shall I know the deviation of the wise, and the judgment of the hypocrite? He said: Truth is light. Beware splitting matters. Some men from the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: Our children are better than us, born upon Islam never associating partners, while we had associated partners. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: We are better than our children, our children are better than their children, and the children of our children are better than the children of their children."
"18407","229 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Yazid ibn Umayrah, who said: When death came to Muadh he said: Seek knowledge with four groups: with Uwaymir Abu al-Darda, with Salman al-Farisi, with Abdullah ibn Masud, and with Abdullah ibn Salam; for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: He is the tenth of ten."
"18408","Al-Harith ibn Umayrah, from Muadh. 230 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram informed, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from the hadith of al-Harith ibn Umayrah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that he said concerning the plague: It is the mercy of your Lord, the supplication of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you."
"18409","231 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from al-Harith ibn Umayrah al-Zubaydi, who said: The plague fell in Syria, and Muadh stood addressing them in Hims, saying: This plague is the mercy of your Lord, the supplication of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you."
"18410","Yazid ibn Husayn, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 232 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiy narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad al-Marwazi narrated, Baqiyyah narrated, from Abi al-Ala al-Dimashqi, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Yazid ibn Husayn, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah never sent a prophet but that in his nation are Qadariyyah and Murjiah who confuse the matter of his nation for him. Verily Allah, Mighty and Majestic, cursed the Qadariyyah and the Murjiah upon the tongues of seventy prophets."
"18411","Hurayth ibn Amr - also said: Umar - from Muadh. 233 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiy narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Abi Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam, Hurayth ibn Umar al-Hadrami narrated to me, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muadh ibn Jabal: Whoever abandons prayer deliberately is free of the protection of Allah."
"18412","234 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, who said: I heard Hurayth ibn Amr al-Hadrami narrating, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Muadh ibn Jabal, whoever abandons prayer is free of protection."
"18413","Abu Zabyah, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 235 - Muhammad ibn Muadh al-Halabi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated, and Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated; both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abi Zabyah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim sleeps upon the remembrance of Allah in purity, then stirs in the night and asks Allah for good of this world and the Hereafter, but He gives it to him. Musa ibn Ismail added: Hammad said: Abu Zabyah passed by us and narrated to us, from Muadh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like thereof."
"18414","Salim ibn Amir al-Khabairi, from Muadh. 236 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-Azhar ibn Abdullah al-Harazi, from Sulaym ibn Amir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man wearing a cloak of silk, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A collar of Fire."
"18415","Shurahbil ibn Mashar al-Absi, from Muadh. 237 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Huti narrated to us, my father narrated, and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi and Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Bakkar narrated to us; they said: Al-Walid ibn Utbah narrated; both said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, Safwan ibn Amr narrated, who said: I heard Shurahbil ibn Mashar narrating, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No servant stands in this world in a station of repute and show but that Allah exposes him before all creatures on the Day of Resurrection."
"18416","238 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Zura, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Shurahbil ibn Mashar al-Absi, he said: I heard Muadh ibn Jabal say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Abdullah ibn Salam is the tenth of ten in Paradise."
"18417","Asim ibn Humayd al-Sakuni, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 239 - Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Asim ibn Humayd al-Sakuni, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: We came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for the Isha prayer and he delayed coming out to us until someone said: He has prayed and will not come out, while a few said: He will come out. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us and said: Pray this prayer late in the night, for you have been favored by it over all other nations, and no one before you ever prayed it."
"18418","240 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abu Salih Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Salih narrated to me, from Malik ibn Ziyad, from Asim ibn Humayd al-Sakuni, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: We came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for the Isha prayer one night, and he delayed it until one might think he had prayed and would not come out. Then he came out afterwards, and someone said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I thought you had prayed and would not come out. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pray this prayer late in the night, for you have been favored by it over all other nations, and no one before you ever prayed it."
"18419","241 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Asim ibn Humayd al-Sakuni, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out with him to bid him farewell, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned toward Madinah and said: These members of my household think they are the most entitled of people, but it is not so; my allies among you are the God-fearing, whoever they are and wherever they are. O Allah, I do not permit them to corrupt what You have set right. By Allah, my ummah will surely be overturned upon its religion as a vessel is overturned in the open ground."
"18420","242 - Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Asim ibn Humayd, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that when he sent him to Yemen he went out with him to bid him farewell, with Muadh riding and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, walking beneath his mount. When he finished he said: O Muadh, perhaps you will not meet me after this year of mine, and perhaps you will pass by my mosque and my grave. So Muadh wept in distress at parting from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Do not weep, O Muadh, for weeping is from Satan."
"18421","Abu al-Munib al-Jurashi, from Muadh. 243 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Abu Munib al-Jurashi, he said: Muadh ibn Jabal addressed us when the plague struck in Sham and said: This matter is the mercy of your Lord, the supplication of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you. O Allah, grant the family of Muadh their share of this matter."
"18422","Shaddad Abu Ammar, from Muadh. 244 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from al-Nahhas ibn Qahm, Shaddad Abu Ammar narrated to us, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Six are among the signs of the Hour: my death, the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis, a man being given a thousand dinars yet resenting it, a tribulation whose heat enters the house of every Muslim, a death that seizes people like the plague of sheep, and that we fight the Romans, who will march with twelve banners, under each banner twelve thousand."
"18423","Abu al-Awwam, caretaker of Bayt al-Maqdis, from Muadh. 245 - Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Malih, from Rawh ibn Aidh, from Abu al-Awwam, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was riding behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a red camel, and he said: O Muadh. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: His right over them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he said: Do you know what the right of the servants upon Allah is when they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Their right upon Him is that He admits them to Paradise."
"18424","Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 246 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Karama narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was traveling with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was on a donkey called Yafur."
"18425","Abu Said al-Himyari, from Muadh. 247 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid informed us, Haywa ibn Shurayh narrated to me, that Abu Said al-Himyari narrated to him, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Guard against the three cursed places: defecating at water sources, on the main road, and in the shade."
"18426","Abdullah ibn Hidhyam, from Muadh. 248 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughba narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us. (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Zurayq ibn Jami al-Misri narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, both said: Rashdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Hidhyam, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he would guard himself from urine and ordered his Companions to do so. Muadh said: Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine. And Ibn Abi Maryam said: From the hadith of Abdullah ibn Hurayth."
"18427","Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 249 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibn Lahia, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Salama ibn Usama, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to collect the charity of the people of Yemen, and ordered me to take from cattle: from every thirty a tabi, from every forty a musinna, from sixty two tabis, from seventy a musinna and a tabi, from eighty two musinnas, from ninety three atabi, from a hundred a musinna and two tabis, from a hundred and twenty three musinnas or four atabi. And he ordered me not to take less than that until it reaches a musinna and a jadhaa. And he said: There is no obligatory due on the awqas. And al-awqas are the young ones."
"18428","Abdullah ibn Yazid Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Muadh. 250 - Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Uqba, meaning Ibn Muslim, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took my hand and said: I love you, O Muadh; do not omit saying in every prayer: O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well. And Ibn Lahia did not mention al-Sunabihi."
"18429","Abu Ayyash, from Muadh. 251 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to me. (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Abu Ayyash, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you wish, I will tell you the first thing Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection: Did you love meeting Me? They will say: Yes, our Lord. He will say: Why? They will say: We hoped for Your mercy and pardon. He will say: My mercy has become obligatory for you."
"18430","Narration of the people of Kufa, from Muadh. Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 252 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him to Yemen and he led them in the dawn prayer and recited al-Nisa. When he reached: And Allah took Ibrahim as a close friend, a woman said: Delighted indeed is the mother of Ibrahim."
"18431","253 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to me, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrating, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him to Yemen and he led them in the dawn prayer, and he mentioned the like of it."
"18432","254 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Do you know, O Muadh, what the right of Allah over people is? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: His right over them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Do you know, O Muadh, what the right of people upon Allah is when they do that? That He does not punish them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not give glad tidings to the people? He said: Leave them to work."
"18433","255 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was riding behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O Muadh, do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is, and what the right of the servants upon Allah is? The right of Allah over His servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him, and the right of the servants upon Allah is that He does not punish whoever dies associating nothing with Him."
"18434","256 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a donkey called Ufayr, and he said to me: O Muadh, do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is? That they worship Him and associate nothing with Him, and the right of the servants upon Allah is that He does not punish whoever associates nothing with Him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not give glad tidings to the people? He said: Do not give them glad tidings lest they rely on it."
"18435","257 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was riding behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is? And he mentioned the hadith."
"18436","Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 258 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Tahir ibn Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Muawiya Amr ibn Abdullah al-Nakhai narrated to us, Abu Amr al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for all that we speak? He said: May your mother lose you, O Muadh ibn Jabal, and what throws people on their nostrils into Hell except the harvests of their tongues?"
"18437","Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 259 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us. (Ha). And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to me in the year two hundred and thirty, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi, from al-Mughira ibn Subayl, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to Yemen, and when I had set out he sent after me and I was brought back. He said: Do you know why I sent for you? Do not take anything without knowledge, for it is misappropriation, and whoever misappropriates will come with what he misappropriated on the Day of Resurrection. For this I called you, so go to your work."
"18438","Masruq ibn al-Ajda, from Muadh. 260 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar and al-Thawri informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him to Yemen, and ordered him to take from every thirty cattle a tabi or tabia, from every forty a musinna, and from every adult a dinar or its equivalent in maafir garments."
"18439","261 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Isa narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq ibn Salama, from Masruq, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to Yemen, and ordered me to take from cattle: from every forty a musinna, from every thirty a tabi or tabia, and from every adult a dinar or its equivalent in maafir."
"18440","262 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi both said: Muhammad ibn Said ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to Yemen, and ordered me to take from every adult a dinar or its equivalent in maafir, and ordered me to take from every thirty cattle a tabi, from every forty a musinna, and ordered me to take from what the sky waters or is watered by rainwater a tenth, and from what is watered by buckets half a tenth."
"18441","263 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him when he sent him to Yemen to take from every thirty cattle a tabi or tabia, from every forty a musinna, and from every adult a dinar or its equivalent in maafir."
"18442","264 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Sufyan and Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Muadh, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"18443","265 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sufyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Hibban, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Salih, from Masruq, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to Yemen, and ordered me to take from cattle: from every thirty a tabi or tabia, and it is the jadha, from every forty a musinna, and from every adult a dinar or its equivalent in maafir garments."
"18444","What Abu Wail Shaqiq ibn Salama narrated, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 266 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Mamar, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Wail, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and in the morning I was close to him while we were traveling, so I said: O Prophet of Allah, will you not tell me of a deed that admits me to Paradise and keeps me away from the Fire? He said: You have asked about a great matter, yet it is easy for whomever Allah makes it easy: you worship Allah associating nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, fast the month of Ramadan, and perform Hajj to the House. Then he said: Shall I not guide you to the gates of goodness? Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and a mans prayer in the depth of the night. Then he recited: Their sides forsake their beds, until he recited: As reward for what they used to do. Then he said: Shall I not tell you of the head of the matter of Islam, its pillar, and the peak of its hump? Jihad. Then he said: Shall I not tell you of what controls all that? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So he took hold of his tongue and said: Restrain this upon you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will we indeed be held accountable for what we speak? He said: May your mother lose you, O Muadh, and what throws people on their faces, or he said: on their nostrils, into the Fire except the harvests of their tongues?"
"18445","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal. Amr ibn Murra, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh. 267 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayra ibn Yarim, from Ali, and from Amr ibn Murra, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, both from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When one of you comes to prayer and the imam is in a state, let him do as the imam does."
"18446","268 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from his elders, from Muadh, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"18447","269 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu Hisham narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"18448","270 - Abu Main Thabit ibn Nuaim al-Hawji narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us. (Ha). And Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, both said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: Prayer was changed through three stages, and fasting was changed through three stages. As for the stages of prayer: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah and prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for seventeen months, then Allah sent down: We see the turning of your face to the heaven, so We shall turn you to a qiblah that pleases you. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned toward the Kaba; this was one stage. They would gather for prayer with some informing others until they nearly adopted the bell. Then a man called Abdullah ibn Zayd came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, let me tell you that I was not asleep, between sleep and wakefulness, I saw a figure wearing two green garments standing, facing the qiblah, saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, until he finished the adhan twice twice, then at the end of his adhan he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah. Then he paused awhile, then stood and said the like of what he said, except he added: The prayer has begun. He said: Teach it to Bilal. So the first to call it was Bilal. And Umar ibn al-Khattab came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the like of what visited Abdullah ibn Zayd visited me, except he beat me to you. These are two stages. They would come to prayer with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, having preceded them in part of the prayer, and they would gesture to them how much he prayed with fingers: one, two. Then Muadh came with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, having preceded him in part of the prayer, and he entered the prayer and said: I do not find him in any state except I am in it, then I make up. Then he came with him having been preceded in part of the prayer and entered the prayer; when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished the prayer, Muadh stood to make up. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Muadh has set a practice for you, so do likewise. These are three stages. As for the stages of fasting: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah and fasted three days each month, and fasted Ashura, and fasted seventeen months from Rabi to the month of Rabi to the month of Ramadan. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, obligated the month of Ramadan upon him, and sent down to him: Fasting is prescribed for you, up to His saying: A ransom of feeding a poor person. So whoever wished fasted, and whoever wished ate and that sufficed him. Then Allah confirmed its fasting upon the resident who is healthy, and gave concession in it to the sick and traveler, and confirmed feeding for the elderly who cannot fast, and sent down to him: The month of Ramadan in which the Quran was sent down as guidance for people and clear proofs of guidance and criterion, so whoever witnesses the month among you let him fast it. They would eat and drink and go to their wives so long as they had not slept; when they slept they abstained from that. Then a man called Sirma spent his day fasting and working, came to his family and slept before breaking fast, and woke fasting. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw him at the end of the day utterly exhausted and said: Why do I see you exhausted? He said: I spent yesterday working, came and slept before breaking fast. And Umar came having gone to his wife after sleeping, and mentioned that to him. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: Permitted for you on the night of fasting is intimacy with your wives, to the end of the verse."
"18449","271 - Abu Zura al-Dimashqi Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Amr ibn Murra al-Jamali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: We would come to prayer, and when a man came having missed part of the prayer, the one next to him would gesture to him: you missed such and such, and he would make it up. So we were between bowing, prostrating, standing, and sitting. One day I came having missed part of the prayer, and I was gestured to as to what I missed. I said: I do not find him in any state except I am in it, so I was in whatever state I found them in. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished, I stood and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, faced the people and said: Who is the one who said such and such? They said: Muadh ibn Jabal. He said: Muadh has set a practice for you, so follow him: when one of you comes having missed part of the prayer, let him pray with the imam his prayer, and when the imam finishes let him make up what he missed."
"18450","272 - Amr ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abu Yahya ibn Sulayman informed me, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: People in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when one of them missed part of the prayer, would ask them and they would gesture to him as to what he missed, so he would pray what he missed, then join them in their prayer. Then Muadh came while the people were sitting in their prayer, and he sat with them. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave salam, he stood and made up what he missed. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do as Muadh ibn Jabal did."
"18451","Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh. 273 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was riding behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said to me: O Muadh, do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: His right over them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he said: Do you know what their right upon Him is when they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Their right upon Him is that He does not punish them."
"18452","274 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us. (Ha). And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me while I was on a donkey, and said: O Muadh, do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is, and what the right of the servants upon Allah is? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The right of Allah over His servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him, and the right of the servants upon Allah when they do that is that He does not punish them."
"18453","275 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Sad ibn Hafs al-Kufi narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O Muadh, do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The right of Allah over His servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he said: Do you know what the right of the servants is when they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That He does not punish them."
"18454","276 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, my uncle Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaida, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you know what the right of Allah over people is? And he mentioned the hadith."
"18455","277 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who met a woman he does not know, and there is nothing a man does with a woman except he did it with her, except he did not have intercourse with her? So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and approaches of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds; that is a reminder for those who remember. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Perform ablution then pray. Muadh said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for him specifically, or for believers generally? He said, three times: Rather it is for believers generally."
"18456","278 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man took from a woman unlawful for him everything a man takes from his wife except he did not have intercourse with her? He said: Perform a good ablution, then stand and pray. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down this verse: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and approaches of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds; that is a reminder for those who remember. Muadh said: Is it for him specifically, O Messenger of Allah, or for Muslims generally? He said: For Muslims generally."
"18457","279 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, all said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed a prayer lengthening its standing, bowing, and prostration. When he finished the prayer we said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed a prayer lengthening its standing, bowing, and prostration? He said: It is a prayer of hope and fear, and I asked my Lord for three things and He gave me two, and withheld one from me: I asked Him not to empower against my ummah an enemy from other than them who would destroy them, and He gave it to me; I asked Him not to destroy them by famine, and He gave it to me; and I asked Him not to place their strife among themselves, and He denied it to me."
"18458","280 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Sad ibn Hafs al-Kufi narrated to us, Shayban Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed a prayer one day lengthening its standing, bowing, and prostration. When he finished I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have prayed a prayer lengthening its standing, bowing, and prostration. He said: It was a prayer of hope and fear; I asked my Lord in it for three things and He gave me two, and withheld one from me: I asked Him not to empower against my ummah an enemy from other than them who would destroy them, and He gave it to me; I asked Him not to empower famine over them so hunger destroys them, and He gave it to me; and I asked Him not to place their strife among themselves, and He denied it to me and withheld it from me."
"18459","281 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Masruqi narrated to us, my uncle Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaida, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed a prayer perfecting its bowing and prostration. And he mentioned the hadith."
"18460","282 - Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The most fearful thing I fear for my ummah is three: the slip of a scholar, the disputation of a hypocrite with the Quran, and worldly life opened up for you."
"18461","283 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The excellence of congregational prayer over a mans prayer alone is twenty-five."
"18462","284 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Ali ibn Mabad narrated to us. (Ha). And Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, both said: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Two men of Banu Israil boasted of lineage in the time of Musa, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one a Muslim and the other a polytheist. The polytheist boasted and said: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, until he counted nine forefathers, then said to his companion: Boast, may you have no mother. He said: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, and I disown what is beyond that. Then Musa called out among the people and gathered them, then said: Judgment has been passed between you two: as for you who traced to nine forefathers, you complete them as the tenth in the Fire; and as for you who traced to your two parents, you are a man of the people of Islam."
"18463","285 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two men of Banu Israil boasted of lineage, one a Muslim and the other a disbeliever. The disbeliever said: You boast. So the disbeliever traced to nine forefathers, and the Muslim said: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, and I disown those above them. Then the crier of Musa, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out: O you two boasters, I have judged between you: as for you, O disbeliever, you traced to nine forefathers, so you are their tenth in the Fire; and as for you, O Muslim, you sufficed with two Muslim parents, so you are of the people of Islam and disown any besides them."
"18464","286 - Abu al-Zinba narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: Two men reviled each other in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with two men present, and one of them became angry until he began rolling in anger. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I know a word that if he said it what he feels of anger would leave. So I drew near to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, what is it, O Prophet? And I wished to know anger, so I drew near to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, what is it, O Prophet of Allah? And I wished to know the outcast one, so I drew near to the man and said it to him but he did not say it, and only grew angrier."
"18465","287 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: Two men boasted of lineage before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and one of them became violently angry. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I know a word that if he said it Allah would remove what he feels. It was said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: What is it? He said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan."
"18466","288 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh, he said: Two men boasted of lineage before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and one of them became angry. He said: I know a word that if he said it his anger would go: I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan."
"18467","289 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaida, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: Two men boasted of lineage before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and one of them became violently angry, so that it seemed to me his nose rolled. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I know a word that if this angry one said it Allah would remove it from him: I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan."
"18468","290 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said al-Qurashi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was late for the dawn prayer until the sun nearly overtook us. Then he came out and led us and shortened his prayer. Then he finished, turned to us with his face, and said: Stay in your places; I will tell you what delayed me from you today in this prayer. I prayed in this night of mine what Allah willed, then sleep overcame my eyes and I slept, and I saw my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, in the finest and most beautiful form. He said: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service, my Lord. He said: Over what does the highest assembly dispute? I said: I do not know. So He placed His palm between my shoulders and I felt the coolness of His fingertips between my breasts, and I knew everything and perceived it. Then He said: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service, my Lord. He said: Over what does the highest assembly dispute? I said: Over expiations. He said: And what are they? I said: Walking on feet to the Friday prayers, perfecting ablution in cold and hardships and degrees. He said: And what is it? I said: Feeding food, gentle speech, and prayer at night while people sleep. He said: Ask. I said: O Allah, I ask You for good deeds, abandoning evils, love of the poor, that You forgive me and have mercy on me, and when You intend tribulation among Your creation, save me to You untempted; and I ask You for Your love, the love of whoever loves You, and love of deeds that bring me near to Your love."
"18469","Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 291 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Fitr ibn Khalifa narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit and al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the expedition of Tabuk, and I saw an empty space and seized it, so I urged my camel toward him until I rode alongside him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a deed that admits me to Paradise. He said: You have asked about a great matter, yet it is easy for whomever Allah makes it easy: you worship Allah associating nothing with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakah, and fast Ramadan. Then he traveled and I traveled. He said: If you wish I will tell you of gates of goodness: fasting is a shield, charity expiates sins, and a mans standing in the depth of the night. Then he recited: Their sides forsake their beds. He said: Then he traveled and I traveled. He said: Shall I not tell you of the head of the matter, its pillar, and the peak of its hump? Jihad in the path of Allah. Then he traveled and I traveled. He said: If you wish I will tell you of what controls people more than all that. There was a brief silence from him, and a glance from me, and I saw a rider and thought he would come and distract him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what controls people more than all that? He gestured with his hand to his tongue. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will we indeed be held accountable for what we speak? He said: May your mother lose you, O Muadh ibn Jabal, and you speak only for or against yourself; and what throws people on their nostrils into the fire of Hell except the harvests of their tongues?"
"18470","292 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us. (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam and Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that admits me to Paradise and keeps me away from the Fire. He said: You asked about a great matter, yet it is easy for whomever Allah makes it easy: you worship Allah associating nothing with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakah, and fast Ramadan; and if you wish I will tell you of the gates of goodness. I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Fasting is a shield, charity expiates sin, and a mans standing in the depth of the night seeking the face of Allah. He said: Then he recited this verse: Their sides forsake their beds. He said: If you wish I will tell you of the head of this matter, its pillar, and the peak of its hump. I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: As for the head of the matter, it is Islam; as for its pillar, it is prayer; as for the peak of its hump, it is jihad in the path of Allah; and if you wish I will tell you of what most controls people. I said: What is it, O Messenger of Allah? He pointed with his finger to his mouth. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will we indeed be held accountable for what we say with our tongues? He said: May your mother lose you, Ibn Jabal, what throws people on their nostrils into the fire of Hell except the harvests of their tongues?"
"18471","293 - Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Qudama al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Zurayq, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Muadh ibn Jabal, the like of it."
"18472","294 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Mansur, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and he mentioned the like of it."
"18473","295 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Hold to good character, for the best of people in character are the best of them in religion."
"18474","296 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Maryam narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Fear Allah wherever you are, follow a bad deed with a good one and it will erase it, and treat people with good character."
"18475","297 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami both said: Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Fear Allah wherever you are. He said: Increase me. He said: Follow a bad deed with a good one and it will erase it, and treat people with good character."
"18476","298 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki both said: Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Fear Allah wherever you are. I said: Increase me. He said: Follow a bad deed with a good one and it will erase it. I said: Increase me. He said: Treat people with good character."
"18477","Abdullah ibn Muslim al-Hadrami, also called Ubayd Allah, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 299 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Yahya ibn al-Jabir, from Ubayd Allah ibn Muslim al-Hadrami, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There are no two Muslims whose three children die except Allah admits both their parents to Paradise by His mercy. They said: And two, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And two. They said: And one, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And one. Then he narrated: The miscarried fetus drags its mother by its umbilical cord to Paradise."
"18478","300 - Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Taymi, from Ubayd Allah ibn Muslim al-Hadrami, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There are no two Muslim women whose three children die except Allah admits both their parents to Paradise by His mercy. I said: What if they are two? He said: And two. I said: What if it is one? He said: And one. Then he said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the miscarried fetus drags its mother by its umbilical cord to Paradise if she seeks reward for it."
"18479","301 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Yahya al-Jabir, from Ubayd Allah ibn Muslim, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"18480","302 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shuba, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Abu Ramla, from Ubayd Allah ibn Muslim, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The father of three has attained obligation. So Muadh ibn Jabal said: And of two, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And of two."
"18481","303 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Taymi, from Abdullah ibn Muslim al-Hadrami, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are no two Muslim women whose three children die in Islam before reaching puberty except Allah admits them to Paradise by His mercy toward them. Muadh said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and two? He said: And two. I said: And one? He said: And one, so that even the miscarried fetus drags its mother by its umbilical cord if she seeks reward for it."
"18482","Urwa ibn al-Nazzal, from Muadh. 304 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from al-Hakam, from Urwa ibn al-Nazzal, or al-Nazzal ibn Urwa, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that admits me to Paradise. He said: Bravo, you have asked about a great matter, yet it is easy for whomever Allah makes it easy: you worship Allah associating nothing with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, and pay the obligatory zakah. Shall I not guide you to the gates of goodness? Or shall I not guide you to the head of the matter, its pillar, and the peak of its hump? As for the head of the matter, it is Islam; whoever submits is safe. As for its pillar, it is prayer. As for the peak of its hump, it is jihad in the path of Allah. Shall I not guide you to the gates of goodness? Fasting is a shield, charity expiates sin, and a servants standing in the depth of the night. And he recited this verse: Their sides forsake their beds. Shall I not tell you of what controls more than that? Then a rider, or riders, approached, and I thought they would distract the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from me. I said: O Messenger of Allah. He said: Shall I not guide you to what controls more than all that? And he pointed with his hand to his tongue. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will we indeed be held accountable for what we speak? He said: May your mother lose you, Muadh, what throws people into the Fire except the harvests of their tongues?"
"18483","305 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Urwa ibn al-Nazzal narrating, from Muadh, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"18484","Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Muadh. 306 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Raja al-Ansari, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking him, and was told: He has gone out. I kept passing no one except he said beforehand: I found him standing praying. When he finished his prayer, I said: You have prayed a long prayer. He said: I prayed with hope and fear; I asked Allah for three things, and He gave me two and denied me one: I asked Him not to destroy my ummah by drowning and He gave it to me; I asked Him not to let an enemy not of them prevail over them and He gave it to me; and I asked Him not to place their strife among themselves and He refused me."
"18485","307 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Raja al-Ansari, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed a prayer one day and lengthened it. When he finished I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have lengthened the prayer today. He said: I prayed a prayer of hope and fear, and asked Allah for my ummah three things; He gave me two and refused one: I asked that He not empower against them an enemy from other than them and He gave it to me; I asked Him not to destroy them by drowning and He gave it to me; and I asked Him not to place their strife among themselves and He refused me."
"18486","Musab ibn Sad, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 308 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, from Musab ibn Sad, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: Umar is indeed of the people of Paradise; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whatever he saw awake or asleep is true, and he said: While I was in Paradise I saw therein a house. I said: Whose is this? It was said: For Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"18487","309 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr, Abu Usama, and Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, all said: Misar informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, from Musab ibn Sad, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: Umar is in Paradise; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And he mentioned the like of it."
"18488","310 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Amash narrating, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, from Musab ibn Sad, that Muadh ibn Jabal said: By Allah, Umar is in Paradise, and I would not like red camels in exchange; you dispersed before I told you why I said that. Then he narrated to them the vision the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw concerning Umar. He said: And the vision of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is true."
"18489","Abu Rifaa, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 311 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ahmad al-Arzami narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Suqa, from Abu Rifaa, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is given from the surplus of what Allah entrusted to me? He said: Begin with your mother, your father, your sister, and your brother, then the nearest, then the nearest; and do not forget the neighbors and the needy."
"18490","Abd Khayr ibn Yazid al-Khaywani, from Muadh. 312 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya narrated to me, Ali ibn Thabit al-Dahhan narrated to us, from Asbat ibn Nasr, from al-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Quran was sent down from seven gates upon seven letters, all healing and sufficient."
"18491","Musa ibn Talha, from Muadh. 313 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiya narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman ibn Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said: I heard Musa ibn Talha say: Muadh ibn Jabal said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him to take from dates, wheat, barley, and raisins. Or he said: grapes."
"18492","314 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, from Talha, from Musa, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, obligated a tenth on grains watered by the sky and rainwater and what springs water; as for watermelon, cucumber, greens, vegetables, pomegranate, and sugarcane, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, exempted them."
"18493","Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 315 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaida, from Abu Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Muadh, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever grows a white hair in Islam, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, he is raised a degree by it."
"18494","Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Muadh. 316 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, Hanifa ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is entrusted with any affair of the Muslims then veils himself from the weak Muslims, Allah will veil Himself from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"18495","al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Muadh. 317 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said to me: O Muadh, do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: They worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he said to me: O Muadh, what is the right of the servants upon Allah when they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That He does not punish them."
"18496","318 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us. (Ha). And al-Hasan ibn Alluya al-Qattan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us, both said: Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Abu Husayn, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a donkey, and he said to me: O Muadh ibn Jabal, what is the right of Allah over His servants? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he said to me: O Muadh, what is the right of the servants upon Allah when they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That He does not punish them."
"18497","319 - Abdullah ibn Najiya narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated to us, from Abu Sad al-Baqqal, from Abu Husayn, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Muadh, do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That you worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Do you know what the right of the servants upon Allah is when they do that? That He does not punish them."
"18498","320 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O Muadh, do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is? And he mentioned the hadith."
"18499","Among those who narrated from him of the people of Hijaz: Aslam, freedman of Umar, from Muadh. 321 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid informed us, Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to me, from Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab went out to the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and there was Muadh ibn Jabal weeping at the grave of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: What makes you weep, O Muadh? He said: Something I heard from the occupant of this grave makes me weep. He said: What is it? He said: I heard him say: A little showing off is polytheism; whoever вражates the allies of Allah has openly fought Allah; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves the hidden God-fearing who when absent are not missed, when present are not invited nor known; their hearts are lamps of guidance; they emerge from every dusty darkness."
"18500","322 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab went out to the mosque one day and found Muadh ibn Jabal weeping at the grave of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned the like of it."
"18501","Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 323 - Abu Awana Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Nasr ibn Marzuq al-Umari narrated to us, Abu Zura Wahb Allah ibn Rashid narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli narrated to us, Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, missed him on Friday. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed, he came to Muadh and said to him: O Muadh, why did I not see you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I owe a Jew an ounce of uncoined gold; I came out to you but he detained me from you. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: O Muadh, shall I not teach you a supplication to supplicate with? If you owed debt like Mount Sabir, Allah would pay it for you, and Sabir is a mountain in Yemen, so supplicate with it, O Muadh: Say: O Allah, Owner of sovereignty, You give sovereignty to whom You will and take sovereignty from whom You will, You honor whom You will and humble whom You will; in Your hand is good; indeed You are over all things competent. You cause the night to enter the day and cause the day to enter the night, You bring the living from the dead and bring the dead from the living, and You provide whom You will without account. Most Merciful of this world and the Hereafter and Most Compassionate to them, You give of them to whom You will and withhold from whom You will; have mercy on me with a mercy that suffices me from the mercy of any besides You."
"18502","Mahmud ibn Labid al-Ansari, from Muadh. 324 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Bakr ibn Bakkar al-Qanabi narrated to me, Mujashi ibn Amr ibn Hassan al-Asadi narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that a son of his died, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote to him consoling him for his son: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to Muadh ibn Jabal: Peace upon you; I praise Allah to you, besides Whom there is no god. To proceed: May Allah magnify your reward, inspire you patience, and grant us and you gratitude. Our selves, wealth, and families are among Allah's pleasant gifts and entrusted loans; He lets enjoy them until a term, and takes them at a known time. We ask Him gratitude for what He gave, and patience when He trials. Your son was among Allah's pleasant gifts and entrusted loans; Allah let you enjoy him in delight and joy, and took him from you with great reward: prayer, mercy, and guidance, if you seek reward for him. So be patient, and let not your distress nullify your reward lest you regret. Know that distress does not bring back a dead one, nor repel grief; and what is coming is as though it has come. And peace."
"18503","Abu Salih al-Samman, from Muadh. 325 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Usayd al-Asbahani narrated to us, Usayd ibn Asim narrated to us, Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, from Hamza al-Zayyat, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Salih, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that he used to pray with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then come to his people and pray with them."
"18504","Abu Abdullah al-Qarrat, from Muadh. 326 - ... narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us ... (Ha). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubayda, Abu Abdullah al-Qarrat narrated to me: I was among the captives taken in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Where are the foremost? They said: Some people went ahead and some stayed behind. He said: Where are the foremost who are infatuated with the remembrance of Allah? Whoever loves to pasture in the gardens of Paradise, let him remember Allah much. And the wording is from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban."
"18505","Ata ibn Yasar, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 327 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Dallal narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever prays these five prayers and fasts the month of Ramadan, I do not know whether he mentioned the zakah of his wealth or not, it is binding upon Allah to forgive him, whether he emigrates or stays where his mother bore him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not go out and inform the people? He said: No, leave people to work; Paradise has a hundred degrees, between every two degrees is like what is between heaven and earth, and its highest degree is al-Firdaws."
"18506","328 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar and Ibn al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned the like of it."
"18507","329 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"18508","330 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Mughira ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever testifies there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishes prayer, gives zakah, and fasts Ramadan, it is binding upon Allah to forgive him. And he mentioned the like of the hadith of Hisham ibn Sad."
"18509","331 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad and Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muadh, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Hold to fear of Allah as much as you can, remember Allah at every stone and tree, and for any evil you do, bring forth to Allah repentance for it: the secret with the secret, and the open with the open."
"18510","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar ibn Jarir al-Ansari, from Muadh. 332 - Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Ramli narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar al-Ansari, from Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man had some right over me, so I feared him, and I sat and stayed two days without going out. Then I went out and came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: O Muadh, what kept you back? I said: A man had a right over me, I feared him until I was ashamed and disliked meeting him. He said: Shall I not command you with words to say, if you owed like mountains Allah would pay it? I said: Yes. He said: Say: O Allah, Owner of sovereignty, You give sovereignty to whom You will and take sovereignty from whom You will, to His saying: Without account, to the end. Most Merciful of this world and the Hereafter and Most Compassionate to them, You give of them to whom You will and withhold of them from whom You will. O Allah, free me from poverty, pay my debt for me, and take me among Your servants in jihad in Your path."
"18511","Sulayman al-Agharr, from Muadh. 333 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqba narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Sulayman al-Agharr, from his father, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If a woman knew the right of the husband, she would not sit while his lunch and dinner are present until he finishes them."
"18512","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amra, from Muadh. 334 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughba narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahia informed us, from Musa ibn Jubayr, that Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Rafi narrated to him, he said: I was in a gathering with Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar, Abdullah ibn Jafar, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amra. Ibn Abi Amra said: I heard Muadh ibn Jabal say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Two words, one of which has no barrier below the Throne, and the other fills what is between heaven and earth: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest. Ibn Umar said to Ibn Abi Amra: Did you hear him say that? He said: Yes. He said: Then Abdullah ibn Umar wept until his beard was soaked with his tears. Then he said: They are two words we cling to and cherish."
"18513","Muhammad ibn Subayh al-Makki, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 335 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Umar ibn Harun narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Subayh, from Muadh, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in a single garment wrapped in it."
"18514","Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Muadh. 336 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to the villages of Arabiyya and ordered me to take the share of the land. Al-Ashjai said: Meaning a third and a quarter."
"18515","Among those who narrated from him of the people of Basra: Abu al-Aswad al-Duali, from Muadh. 337 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Burayda, from Abu al-Aswad al-Duali, he said: I said to Muadh ibn Jabal: Tell me about the story of the Satan when you seized him. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, put me in charge of the charity of the Muslims, so I placed it in a room. And he mentioned the hadith."
"18516","338 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shuba, from Amr ibn Abi Hakim, from Abdullah ibn Burayda, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Duali, he said: Muadh was in Yemen and they brought to him the case of a Jew who died leaving his Muslim brother. Muadh said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Islam increases and does not decrease. So he gave him the inheritance."
"18517","339 - Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Hakim, from Abdullah ibn Burayda, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Duali, he said: A man of us died a Jew or Christian leaving a Muslim son, so that was raised to Muadh and he gave him the inheritance. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Islam increases and does not decrease."
"18518","340 - Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Salih al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Amr ibn Kurdi, from Yahya ibn Yamar, that Muadh ibn Jabal would give the Muslim inheritance from the dhimmi, and would not give the dhimmi inheritance from the Muslim. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Islam increases and does not decrease. The shaykh said: Amr ibn Kurdi is Amr ibn Abi Hakim from whom Shuba narrated."
"18519","Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 341 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Nadra, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that he was ill and spat to his right, or intended to spit to his right, and said: I have not spat to my right since I became Muslim."
"18520","Abu Malih ibn Usama al-Hudhali, from Muadh. 342 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Abu Burda, from Abu Malih, from Muadh ibn Jabal and Abu Musa, both said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I reserve my intercession for whoever dies associating nothing with Allah."
"18521","343 - Abu Umar al-Darir Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Said al-Kufi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Burda, from his father, and from Abu al-Malih, from Muadh ibn Jabal, both said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, traveled, the Emigrants nearest him would be around him. One night we missed him from his place and feared something had befallen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. We went seeking him and there was a commotion like the grinding of a millstone; we met him returning. I said: We missed you, O Messenger of Allah, and feared something had befallen you. He said: No, but a messenger from my Lord came to me and gave me choice between half my ummah entering Paradise or intercession, so I chose intercession. We said: We ask you by the right of Islam and by the right of our companionship that you include us in it. He said: You are in it. Then two men came and said the like of that, and he said to them: Yes. Then another came, until people multiplied. He said: I place in my intercession whoever of my ummah dies associating nothing with Allah."
"18522","al-Ala ibn Ziyad al-Adawi, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 344 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Hurr, from al-Qasim, from al-Ala ibn Ziyad, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Satan is the wolf of man like the wolf of sheep; he seizes the distant and straying one. Beware of mountain paths; hold to the generality, the congregation, and the mosques."
"18523","345 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Ala ibn Ziyad, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would say: Satan is the wolf of man like the wolf of sheep; he seizes the straying sheep, the distant, and the isolated."
"18524","346 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Ala ibn Ziyad, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no supplication more beloved to Allah for a servant to supplicate Him with than to say: O Allah, I ask You for well-being in this world and the Hereafter."
"18525","Tawus al-Yamani, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 347 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ibrahim ibn Maysara, from Tawus, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: They asked him about less than thirty cattle and about honey. He said: I was not ordered anything concerning them."
"18526","348 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hakam ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not tell me anything about the awqas of cattle."
"18527","349 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Tawus, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no divorce in what one does not own, and no emancipation in what one does not own."
"18528","350 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Tawus, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"18529","351 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Tawus, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There is no divorce for what one does not own, and no emancipation for what one does not own."
"18530","352 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us. (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, both said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Muadh, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No son of Adam does a deed more saving for him from the punishment of Allah than the remembrance of Allah. They said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah? He said: No, unless you strike with your sword until it breaks. Three times."
"18531","353 - Ahmad ibn Said ibn Urwa al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Khalid al-Ahmar say: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Tawus, from Muadh, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not hasten tribulation before it descends; draw near and be upright, for if you hasten it before it descends, the flood will carry you here and there."
"18532","Unnamed men, from Muadh. 354 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said al-Asbahani narrated to us, Uqba ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ibrahim, my father narrated to us, from al-Saluli, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If I take a pulpit, my father Ibrahim already took one; and if I take the staff, my father Ibrahim, peace be upon him, already took it."
"18533","355 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yazid ibn Iyad informed me, from Musa ibn Muhammad al-Taymi, from Ibn Shihab, from al-Balawi, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If slavery were ever established upon any Arab it would be today; it is only captivity or ransom."
"18534","356 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from a man, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There is nothing due on the awqas."
"18535","357 - Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Hawti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musab al-Qarqasani narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Jabir al-Tai, from a man, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever equips a warrior or succeeds him among his family with good is with us."
"18536","358 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jafar, from Hisham, from a man narrating, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There are men who are neither prophets nor martyrs for whom pulpits of light will be placed on the Day of Resurrection; their faces of light, secure on the Day of Resurrection from the greatest terror. A man said: O Prophet of Allah, who are they? He said: They are those uprooted from tribes, loving one another in Allah."
"18537","359 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn al-Rabi al-Yuhmidi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn al-Daylami, he said: I was the third of three serving Muadh ibn Jabal. When death approached him we said to him: May Allah have mercy on you, we accompanied you, devoted ourselves to you, and followed you for this day; narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that we may benefit. He said: Yes, and this is no time for lying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever dies certain of three: that Allah is true, that the Hour is coming, and that Allah will resurrect those in graves. And Ibn Sirin said: I forgot whether he said: He enters Paradise, or he said: He is saved from the Fire."
"18538","360 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Artat ibn al-Mundhir, from al-Abahh al-Sakuni, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever dies associating nothing with Allah, Paradise is obligatory for him."
"18539","361 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir al-Bakhtari al-Tai narrated to us, Bishr ibn Shuayb ibn Abi Hamza narrated to us, from his father, from al-Zuhri, some people of knowledge narrated to us, that Muadh ibn Jabal would narrate that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the distance between the edge of the Fire and its bottom is a rock the weight of seven pregnant camels with their fat, meat, and offspring, falling between the edge of the Fire until it reaches its bottom for seventy autumns."
"18540","Mursal reports, from Muadh ibn Jabal. 362 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Awn al-Thaqafi, from al-Harith ibn Amr, nephew of al-Mughira ibn Shuba, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him to Yemen, he said to him: How will you judge if a case presents itself? He said: I judge by the Book of Allah. He said: If it is not in the Book of Allah? He said: Then by the practice of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: If it is not in the practice of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: I exert my opinion and spare no effort. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck his chest and said: Praise be to Allah who guided the messenger of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to what pleases the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"18541","363 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Haywa ibn Shurayh informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Salama ibn Usama, from Yahya ibn al-Hakam, that Muadh ibn Jabal said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me as collector to the people of Yemen, and ordered me to take from cattle: from every thirty a tabi, and the tabi is the jadha, or a tabia; from every forty a musinna. He said: They offered me to take what is between forty and fifty, between sixty and seventy, and between eighty and ninety. I refused them and said to them: Until I ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that. I came and informed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he ordered me to take from every thirty a tabi, from forty a musinna, from sixty two tabias, from seventy a musinna and a tabi, from eighty two musinnas, from ninety three atabi, from a hundred a musinna and two tabis, from a hundred and ten two musinnas and a tabi, from a hundred and twenty three musinnas or four atabi. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered me not to take anything from between that until it reaches a musinna or jadha. He also claimed that the awqas have no obligatory due."
"18542","364 - Ghaylan ibn Abd al-Samad al-Tayalisi Maghamma narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubayda, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, he said: When Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah was struck in the plague of Amwas, he appointed Muadh ibn Jabal as successor. The pain intensified and people said: O Muadh, supplicate Allah to lift this punishment from us. He said: It is not a punishment, but the supplication of your Prophet, the death of the righteous before you, and a martyrdom by which Allah singles out whom He wills among you."
"18543","365 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Bara ibn Abdullah al-Ghanawi narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan narrating, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: When death approached him he wept. They said: What makes you weep? He said: By Allah, I do not weep in distress from death, nor for a world I leave behind, but I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: They are but two handfuls: a handful in the Fire and a handful in Paradise, and I do not know of which handful I am."
"18544","366 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Humayd ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abu Tariq al-Sadi narrated to me, he said: I witnessed al-Hasan at his death dictating, saying to the scribe: Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; this is what al-Hasan testified: he testified there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah truthfully from his heart; whoever testifies to it at his death truthfully enters Paradise. I heard that from Muadh ibn Jabal, who enjoined it at his death, narrating it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"18545","367 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, he said: I heard my father mention, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, by Him who sent you with truth, something presents itself in my breast; to be charred coal is dearer to me than to utter it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Praise be to Allah; Satan has despaired of being worshipped in this land of mine, but he is content with the belittled of your deeds."
"18546","368 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, al-Nahhas ibn Qahm narrated to us, from Shaddad Abu Ammar, from Muadh, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Six are among the signs of the Hour: my death, the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis, a death that seizes people as the plague that seizes sheep, a man being given a thousand dinars yet resenting it, a tribulation whose fear enters the heart of every Muslim, and that the Romans attack us marching with eighty banners."
"18547","369 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi narrated to us, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Abdullah al-Shami, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from Makhul, raised to Muadh ibn Jabal, and Muadh raised it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Keep your mosques clear of your children, disputes, penalties, buying and selling; perfume them on Fridays, and place your purification facilities at their doors."
"18548","370 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Malik al-Lakhmi, from Makhul, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Obey every commander, pray behind every imam, and do not revile any of my Companions."
"18549","371 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us. (Ha). And Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Razin, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not guide you to a treasure of the treasures of Paradise? I said: Yes. He said: There is no power nor strength except in Allah."
"18550","372 - Muhammad ibn Muadh al-Halabi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Razin, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a camel with a packsaddle fastened on it, and said: O Muadh. I said: At your service and happiness. He said: Do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: His right over them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he said: Do you know what the right of the servants upon Allah is when they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Their right upon Him when they do that is that He forgives them and admits them to Paradise."
"18551","373 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Muadh, that he came from Yemen. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I came from people some of whom prostrate to others; shall we not do that for you? He said: If I were to order a human to prostrate to a human, I would order women to prostrate to their husbands."
"18552","374 - Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salama, he said: Muadh ibn Jabal said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Worship Allah as though you see Him, count yourself among the dead, remember Allah, Mighty and Majestic, at every stone and tree, and when you do an evil deed do a good deed beside it: the secret with the secret, and the open with the open. Then he said: Shall I not tell you of what most controls people? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He took the edge of his tongue. I said: O Messenger of Allah, as though belittling it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What throws people on their nostrils into the Fire except this? And he took the edge of his tongue."
"18553","375 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Habib ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him to Yemen. When he came to them he said: O people, I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to you, telling you that the return is to Allah, to Paradise or Fire; eternity without death, residence without departing."
"18554","Muadh ibn al-Harith al-Ansari of Badr, and he is Ibn Afra, and Afra is his mother. 376 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Bakkai, from Ibn Ishaq, in naming those who witnessed Badr: Muadh ibn Afra, and he is Muadh ibn al-Harith ibn Rifaa ibn Sawda ibn Malik ibn Ghanm ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar, and Afra is his mother, and she is the mother of Awf and Muawwidh; all witnessed Badr. And Afra is the daughter of Ubayd ibn Thalaba ibn Ghanm ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar."
"18555","377 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Nasr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muadh ibn Afra, that he would circumambulate the House, and circumambulated after Asr and did not pray. Muadh, a man of Quraysh, said to him: What prevents you from praying? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbidding prayer after two prayers: after dawn until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."
"18556","378 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Nasr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his grandfather Muadh al-Qurashi, that he circumambulated the House with Muadh ibn Afra after Asr and after dawn, and did not pray. He asked him and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no prayer after two prayers: after dawn until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."
"18557","379 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad informed us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, that he heard Nasr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating, from his grandfather Muadh, a man of Banu Taym, that he would circumambulate after Asr with Muadh ibn Afra and did not pray. I said: What prevented you from praying? He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade prayer at two times: after dawn until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."
"18558","Muadh ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh al-Ansari then al-Khazraji of Badr, and he is the killer of Abu Jahl ibn Hisham. 380 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakkai narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, in naming those who witnessed Badr of the Ansar, then of Khazraj: Muadh ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh ibn Zayd ibn Haram ibn Kab ibn Ghanm ibn Kab ibn Salama ibn Sad ibn Ali ibn Asad ibn Sarida, also said: Sadira, also said: Tazid ibn Hushaym ibn al-Khazraj, witnessed Badr, killed Abu Jahl, Ikrima ibn Abi Jahl cut his hand, then he lived until the time of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him."
"18559","381 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, from Salih ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: While I was standing in the rank on the day of Badr, I looked to my right and left, and there I was between two youths of the Ansar of tender age. I wished to be between sturdier than them. One of them nudged me and said: O uncle, do you know Abu Jahl? I said: Yes; what need have you of him, O son of my brother? He said: I was told he reviles the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if I see him my shadow will not part from his until the sooner of us dies. I marveled at that. The other nudged me and said the like to me. It was not long before I saw Abu Jahl moving among the people. I said to them: This is your man you ask about. They rushed at him with their swords and struck him until they killed him. Then they went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told him. He said: Which of you killed him? Each of them said: I killed him. He said: Have you wiped your swords? They said: No. He looked at the two swords and said: Both of you killed him. He awarded his spoils to Muadh ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh. And they were Muadh ibn Afra and Muadh ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh."
"18560","Muadh Abu Zuhayr al-Thaqafi. 382 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Shurayh ibn al-Numan narrated to us. (Ha). And Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf, the two Egyptians, narrated to us, both said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar informed me. (Ha). And al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, and Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, all said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us. (Ha). And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, all said: Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us, Umayya ibn Safwan narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Thaqafi, from his father Abu Zuhayr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say in his sermon at al-Nabaah, or al-Nabawa, of Taif: You are about to know the people of Paradise from the people of Fire, or your best from your worst. Nafi said: I only know he said: The people of Paradise from the people of Fire. A man among the people said: By what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: By good praise and bad praise; you are witnesses, some of you over others."
"18561","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Umayya ibn Yala al-Thaqafi narrated, from his father, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Zuhayr, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you give names, give names of servitude to Allah."
"18562","Muadh ibn Anas al-Juhani. Bishr ibn Musa al-Asadi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sitting with the knees drawn up and wrapped in a garment on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon."
"18563","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drawing up the knees in a wrapped garment on Friday."
"18564","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas narrated to me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives up fine clothing while he is able to afford it, out of humility for Allah the Mighty and Majestic, Allah will call him before all creatures on the Day of Resurrection until He gives him the choice of the robes of faith, to wear whichever of them he wishes."
"18565","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym Dirar ibn Surad narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives up fine clothing out of humility while he is able to afford it, Allah will call him before all creatures on the Day of Resurrection until he is given the choice of the garments of Paradise, to wear whichever of them he wishes."
"18566","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18567","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever eats food and says: Praise be to Allah who fed me this and provided me with it without any power or strength on my part, Allah will forgive him his past sins; and whoever wears a garment and says: Praise be to Allah who clothed me with this and provided me with it without any power or strength on my part, Allah will forgive him his past sins."
"18568","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Nafi ibn Yazid informed us, Abu Marhum narrated, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, that a man came to a gathering in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present and said: Peace be upon you, so he returned the greeting and said: Ten good deeds. Then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, so he said: Twenty. Then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, so he said: Forty. And he said: This is how the extra reward is."
"18569","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted said: My servant does not remember Me to himself except that I remember him among an assembly of My angels, and he does not remember Me in an assembly except that I remember him in the Highest Company."
"18570","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18571","Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18572","Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Utter harshness, disbelief and hypocrisy is that one who hears the caller of Allah calling to prayer and inviting to success and does not answer him."
"18573","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), exactly the same."
"18574","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Enough misery and failure for a believer that he hears the mu'adhdhin announcing the prayer and does not answer him."
"18575","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever recites: Say, He is Allah, the One, ten times, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise. So Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Then we will seek an abundance, O Messenger of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greater and Better."
"18576","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18577","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites a thousand verses in the path of Allah will be written on the Day of Resurrection among the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs and the righteous, and excellent are those as companions."
"18578","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18579","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Nafi ibn Yazid informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Usayd, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites a thousand verses in the path of Allah, Allah will write him among the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs and the righteous."
"18580","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever guards behind the Muslims in the path of Allah voluntarily, with no ruler compelling him, his eyes will not see the Fire except for the passing that fulfills the oath, for Allah the Exalted says: There is none of you but will come to it."
"18581","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18582","Azhar ibn Zufar al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, Khayr ibn Nu'aym al-Hadrami the judge narrated, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remembrance of Allah is a hundred times more excellent than spending in the path of Allah."
"18583","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated, and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated; both said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated, Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Remembrance of Allah in the path of Allah is multiplied seven hundred times over spending."
"18584","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"18585","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah, that a man asked him: Which of those who strive in jihad has the greatest reward? He said: Those of them who remember Allah the most. He said: And which of those who fast has the greatest reward from Allah? He said: Those of them who remember Allah the most. Then he mentioned prayer, zakat, hajj and charity, and in each case the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those of them who remember Allah the most. So Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said to Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: O Abu Hafs, those who remember Allah have carried off all good. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes indeed."
"18586","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is a duty on one who rises from a gathering to greet them with peace, and a duty on one who comes to a gathering to greet them with peace. Then a man stood while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was speaking, and he did not give the greeting of peace, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How quickly he forgot."
"18587","Abdullah ibn Wahb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"18588","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever constructs a building without injustice or aggression, or plants a planting without injustice or aggression, it will be a continuing reward for him as long as any of the creation of Allah the Mighty and Majestic benefits from it."
"18589","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym Dirar ibn Surad narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever constructs a building without injustice or aggression, its reward belongs to him as long as any of the creation of the Most Merciful, the Mighty and Majestic, benefits from it."
"18590","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever gives for the sake of Allah, withholds for the sake of Allah, loves for the sake of Allah and hates for the sake of Allah has perfected his faith."
"18591","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah who said: The best of virtues is that you join ties with one who cut you off, give to one who deprived you, and pardon one who reviled you."
"18592","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"18593","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever suppresses anger while he is able to carry it out, Allah will call him before all creatures until He gives him the choice of which of the wide-eyed houris he wishes; and whoever refrains from wearing good clothes while he is able to afford them, out of humility for Allah the Mighty and Majestic, Allah will call him before all creatures until Allah gives him the choice of which of the robes of faith he wishes."
"18594","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"18595","Wathila ibn al-Hasan al-Irqi narrated to us, Kathir ibn Ubayd al-Hadhdha narrated, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Adham, who said: I heard a man narrating, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Farwa ibn Mujahid, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever suppresses anger while able to carry it out, Allah will give him the choice of the wide-eyed houris on the Day of Resurrection; whoever leaves off a garment of beauty while able to wear it, Allah will clothe him with the robe of faith; and whoever marries off a servant for the sake of Allah, Allah will place upon his head the crown of kingship."
"18596","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever steps over the Muslims on Friday takes a bridge to Hell."
"18597","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: The one who laughs in prayer, the one who turns, and the one who cracks his fingers are of the same standing."
"18598","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who turns in prayer, the one who laughs, and the one who cracks his fingers are of the same standing."
"18599","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: That I escort a warrior in the path of Allah and help him in a morning or evening expedition is more beloved to me than the world and all it contains."
"18600","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
